// Fate's Whimsy (Universal Spell, cost 1, DE common) -- "Play only after any player rolls one or
// more dice. Re-roll one of those dice. Choose which result to use. You may play this Spell on
// any player's turn."
//
// Category D SEVENTH item, 2026-08-12, task #724. The card that motivated the entire
// mid-die-roll pause infrastructure -- see `effects.ts#requestDieRoll` and `rollConsumers.ts`
// for the shared machinery, and `state.pendingDieRoll`'s own field-level doc comment for the
// data-shape contract.
//
// OWNER RULINGS (2026-08-12) that shaped this build:
//   Q2: One die per Whimsy play. This engine's real cards all use single-die rolls (all 43
//       rollDie/rollDieWithRerolls call sites are single-die), so "reroll ONE of those dice"
//       reduces to "reroll THE die." A future multi-die card would need Whimsy to prompt for
//       WHICH die -- the mechanism supports it (pendingDieRoll.currentValue is a single number
//       today; would become an array + index picker), but no build work needed today.
//   Q3: Chainable, with the simplified read: after each Whimsy play + player pick, current value
//       re-arms the window for any player who still has a legal Whimsy in hand (including the
//       just-played player if they hold another copy). Loop until nobody plays. `play.ts`'s
//       `resolveFateWhimsyChoice` implements this by re-computing `eligibleReactorPlayerIds`
//       via `findFateWhimsyEligibleReactors` after each choice, so a Whimsy played and moved to
//       the discard pile naturally drops that copy out of eligibility.
//   Q4: Reroll goes through the SAME pipeline as the original roll -- `rollDieWithRerolls` (so
//       Loaded Dice / Emec's Tinker still fire) and `dieRollBonus` (so Pyte's Luck still applies
//       its +1). Handled here by calling `rollDieWithRerolls` on the reroll, same as
//       `requestDieRoll` uses for the original roll. Each Whimsy play only rerolls ONCE (no
//       infinite recursion): the Whimsy machine's own choice-arming step opens a NEW window
//       for any OTHER Whimsy play, not for Whimsy on its own reroll mid-choice.
//   Q5: Applies to ALL die-roll contexts. All rollDie call sites are being refactored to
//       requestDieRoll in Phase 3.
//
// Eye of the Storm's "you cannot use other cards to alter the die roll" is honored via the
// declarative-static `dieRollCannotBeAltered: boolean` field on `CardEffectDefinition` --
// `requestDieRoll` fast-paths (invokes the consumer inline, skipping the Whimsy window entirely)
// whenever the SOURCE of the roll carries that flag.
//
// The Spell itself has NO `resolveSpell` body of the shape most cards have -- Fate's Whimsy's
// effect isn't "do X during resolution," it's "play THIS Spell as a reactive response to open
// die-roll window." All the mechanics live in `play.ts#playFateWhimsy`, which is the entry point
// `Play.tsx` calls when a player picks the Whimsy prompt. This file just registers the card so
// `isCardImplemented('Fate\'s Whimsy')` returns true and so a future doc-generation sweep sees a
// real entry rather than an unimplemented stub.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect("Fate's Whimsy", {
  // No hooks -- see the header for why the mechanics live in play.ts#playFateWhimsy instead.
});
