// Glablit -- two printed Effects:
//   "Dream Blur: All of your Bograth Creatures in play are also Core. All of your Core Creatures
//   in play are also Bograth."
//   "Shifty: Glablit loses no energy from opposing Effects."
//
// Neither Effect has a card-side hook. Both are handled by the shared engine plumbing they're
// meant to trigger:
//   * Shifty: effects.ts's discardEnergy checks printsShifty on the target and zeroes out any
//     'effect'-caused loss when the target is opposing. Zero registration needed.
//   * Dream Blur: targeting.ts's effectiveRegions checks the controller's inPlay for a
//     non-locked-down Glablit AND augments any Creature's regions with the OTHER of Bograth/Core
//     whenever one of them is present in the effective (post-override) region list. Category D
//     EIGHTH item, 2026-08-12, task #725, closed the architectural gap this file's earlier
//     "deferred" comment described.
//
// This file just registers Glablit's presence in the registry (an empty entry would otherwise
// report as "not implemented" via isCardImplemented).

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Glablit', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (deep-dive audit, 2026-08-13). Both Effects are handled by
  // shared engine plumbing (no per-card hook body): Dream Blur by targeting.ts's
  // effectiveRegions (Category D closure 2026-08-12), Shifty by effects.ts's discardEnergy
  // check against JSON-data-driven printsShifty. Listed as `[]` per the E5 Shifty convention.
  effectHooks: {
    'Dream Blur': [],
    Shifty: [],
  },
});
