// Sabertooth Jumbor -- "Weave: Whenever Sabertooth Jumbor attacks or is attacked, before energy
// is removed, you may move up to one energy between it and one of your other Naroom or Weave
// Creatures in play." (see weave.ts)
// "Taunt (1): Use this Power only before your Attack step. Until the beginning of your next turn,
// all Creatures must attack, if able, and all of your Creatures in play gain one energy in
// attacks after energy is removed."
//
// The must-attack half is task #44 Part B (2026-07-18, must-attack enforcement architecture) --
// "all Creatures" has no "your"/"opposing" qualifier (unlike the SECOND clause, which explicitly
// says "your"), so it tags EVERY Creature currently in play on BOTH sides, expiry
// `beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber` (matches this exact "until the beginning of your next turn"
// wording, durationTags.ts's own precedent).
//
// The +1-in-attacks half (RESOLVED, multi-region deferred-list re-audit Bucket C, 2026-08-13,
// owner Q&A the same day) arms `PlayerState.sabertoothTauntUntilTurn` -- same
// "PlayerState-field-checked-generically-in-combat.ts" shape as Creeping Chill / Sneak Attack /
// Scarletsong's Trill / Aglow, and for the same reason: the +1 must keep firing for the printed
// "until the beginning of your next turn" window even if Jumbor itself leaves play mid-window, so
// it can't hang off Jumbor's own in-play card. Owner rulings resolving the three deferred Qs:
//
//   Q1. "In attacks" = BOTH attacker and defender (project convention -- "in attacks" is always
//       both-sided; "when it attacks" / "when it is attacked" would be the one-sided wording).
//   Q2. "After energy is removed" = AFTER the zero-energy defeat sweep. A Creature that hit 0 in
//       this attack is already defeated -- no +1 save.
//   Q3. Direct-Magi attacks DO grant the attacker +1 (what a Creature is attacking doesn't
//       dictate whether it gains energy; the printed text is "your Creatures in play gain one
//       energy in attacks," which the attacking Creature satisfies regardless of target).
//
// The actual +1 lives in combat.ts, applied right after `checkForDefeats` at step 8 so a defeated
// Creature never receives it (Q2), with independent checks for attacker and defender each gated on
// THAT Creature's own controller's window (Q1) and unconditional-on-defender for the attacker so
// direct-Magi attacks are covered (Q3). Multiple Sabertooth Jumbors on one board don't stack --
// the field is a per-controller expiry, so re-arming just overwrites with the same value.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { applyWeave } from './weave.js';
import { allCreaturesInPlay } from '../targeting.js';
import { addDurationTag, MUST_ATTACK_THIS_TURN, beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Sabertooth Jumbor', {
  legalPhases: ['prs1'],
  weaveConfig: { eligibleRegions: ['Naroom', 'Weave'], mode: 'both' },
  onBeforeEnergyRemoved: (ctx, self) => applyWeave(ctx, self, ['Naroom', 'Weave']),
  resolvePower: (ctx) => {
    if (ctx.powerName !== 'Taunt') return;
    const expiry = beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
    for (const creature of allCreaturesInPlay(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb)) {
      addDurationTag(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, creature, MUST_ATTACK_THIS_TURN, expiry);
    }
    // Second clause: arm the controller's own +1-in-attacks window (see file header for owner
    // Q1-Q3 answers). The actual +1 gain lives in combat.ts, checked generically after
    // `checkForDefeats` so a defeated Creature never receives it.
    ctx.controllingPlayer.sabertoothTauntUntilTurn = expiry;
  },
});
