// Gate to Ombor -- "Guard (2): Search your deck for one of your Magi's starting Creatures. Play
// that Creature, reducing its cost by five energy, to a minimum of zero. That Creature can never
// attack." "Reducing its cost" is a discount on what's PAID to play it, not a cut to its starting
// energy -- play.ts's own playCard already treats "cost paid" and "starting energy" as distinct
// concepts for Creatures (a region penalty inflates what's paid without inflating starting energy,
// per its comment: "starting energy = the card's own cost, never the region-penalty-inflated
// total"), so a cost REDUCTION should symmetrically leave starting energy at its full printed
// value too -- only the payment shrinks. The reduced amount is paid from the Magi (no other payer
// is named in the text, and this Power's own cost is separately paid via the normal Power-cost
// step). Same "search for a starting card" filter as Ythra's Mantle. Tags the played Creature with
// the PERMANENT (not this-turn) CANNOT_ATTACK -- combat.ts's isLegalAttack now checks
// tags.has(CANNOT_ATTACK) in addition to the duration-tag version, same split isIllusion already
// uses.
//
// "Gate to Ombor cannot be discarded from play by opposing cards that specifically discard Relics
// from play. Discard Gate to Ombor from play if your Magi is not an Underneath Magi." -- built via
// registry.ts's `canBeDiscardedFromPlay` hook + the shared regionLockedRelic.ts helper (same
// shape as Kybar's Fang/Vault of Knowledge Key/Gift of the Weave) -- turned out to be a narrow,
// self-contained hook rather than needing task #26's full passive-Relic-text system.
//
// "Talisman: If you have an Amulet of Ombor in play, you can play Gate to Ombor from your hand or
// from your deck, ignoring all costs. Add one to all die rolls you make for Amulet of Ombor (die
// rolls of 6 remain 6)." -- BUILT (Bucket C closure, deferred-list full re-audit, Underneath
// region pass, 2026-08-13). Owner rulings that unblocked this pass, in the order the questions
// were asked:
//
//   Q1 (my question was malformed) -- owner clarified: Gate to Ombor is a RELIC, not a Creature.
//   Standard relic rules apply: you can't play a relic that's already on your side of the field.
//   Talisman only changes WHERE it can be played from (hand OR deck) and the COST (zero, when
//   Amulet of Ombor is in play). It does NOT change when it can be played (standard timing rules
//   apply) or who may play it.
//   Q2 (usage count) -- basic game mechanics: can't have multiple copies in play on your side.
//   If Gate to Ombor left the field (must be by your OWN effect -- Gate cannot be discarded by
//   opposing cards, per the immunity clause above), you may use Talisman again. Cannot use
//   Talisman if Gate to Ombor is already in play on your side.
//   Q3 (onPlay broadcast) -- YES. Card text says "you can PLAY Gate to Ombor" -- it's a real
//   play. `onPlay` fires. (Owner note: "This 'precedent' [of syntheticPowers not firing onPlay]
//   has constantly needed to be retrofitted to work correctly. This should NOT be the default. If
//   a card is being played or entering play, it should be treated as such unless very
//   specifically being told not to in the card text." -- baseline for future play-from-elsewhere
//   hooks.)
//   Q4 (luckContext widen) -- YES. Scope to only rolling for Amulet's die-roll Power (Gate's +1
//   bonus). Widen luckContext to receive the rolling source instance so a card-name-scoped die
//   bonus is expressible.
//
// Implementation shape (both subclauses):
//
// SUBCLAUSE 1 -- "play from hand or deck, ignoring all costs" while Amulet of Ombor is in play.
// Split cleanly across two existing/one new engine mechanism:
//   (a) COST = 0 via `selfCostOverride` (registry.ts): shipped for the Shadow Geysers'
//       "cost is zero if..." family; a TOTAL override, not a floored delta, so it can express a
//       genuine 0 for a 6-cost Relic. Applies to both the hand play and the deck play (`playCard`
//       and `resolvePlayableFromDeck` both go through `isLegalToPlay`, which reads it).
//   (b) FROM HAND -- no new plumbing needed. With `selfCostOverride` returning 0 and standard
//       "player's own turn, Relic phase, no duplicate relic" legality applied by `isLegalToPlay`,
//       playing Gate to Ombor from hand is a plain `playCard` call.
//   (c) FROM DECK -- new `offersPlayFromDeck` / `onPlayedFromDeck` hooks (registry.ts) +
//       `previewPlayableFromDeck` / `resolvePlayableFromDeck` (play.ts), mirroring the existing
//       `offersPlayFromDiscardPile` / `previewPlayableFromDiscardPile` /
//       `resolvePlayableFromDiscardPile` triple that shipped for Brushfire / Sand Cape's Memory.
//       Reuses `playFromZonePayingCost` widened to accept 'deck' as a source zone;
//       `resolvePlayableFromDeck` opts OUT of the usual phase-gate bypass (owner Q1 -- standard
//       timing), so it goes through `isLegalToPlay` unchanged and picks up the duplicate-relic
//       check for free.
//   Q2 is naturally handled: the standard duplicate-relic block in `isLegalToPlay` (play.ts's
//   "You already have a copy of X in play") rejects a second Gate to Ombor on the same side --
//   the offer itself also guards on "no Gate in play on my side" for a clean UI signal, but the
//   backstop is the shared legality check, not a new bespoke gate.
//   Q3 is naturally handled: both `playCard` and `resolvePlayableFromDeck` (via
//   `playFromZonePayingCost`) funnel through the normal card-enters-play sequencing, which
//   includes the `broadcastCardEnteredPlay` onPlay dispatch. No opt-out.
//
// SUBCLAUSE 2 -- "add one to all die rolls you make for Amulet of Ombor (die rolls of 6 remain
// 6)". Registers `addsToOwnDieRolls`; body filters on `rollingSource.definitionKey` matching
// Amulet of Ombor's key (the new 4th arg widened per owner Q4). Clamp at 6 is inherited free
// from `rollDie`'s existing `Math.min(sides, raw + bonus)` -- Pyte's own "maximum of six" clamp
// was already the exact shape Talisman needs.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { effectiveStartingEnergy } from '../targeting.js';
import { playFromZone } from '../effects.js';
import { shuffleDeck } from '../zones.js';
import { addPermanentTag, CANNOT_ATTACK } from '../durationTags.js';
import { applyRegionLockedRelic } from './regionLockedRelic.js';
import type { GameState, PlayerId } from '../types/state.js';
import type { CardDatabase } from '../types/card.js';

const GATE_TO_OMBOR_NAME = 'Gate to Ombor';
const AMULET_OF_OMBOR_NAME = 'Amulet of Ombor';

/** True when `playerId` currently has at least one Amulet of Ombor in play (own inPlay only --
 *  Amulet is a Relic, only ever on its own controller's side). Shared by every Talisman hook so
 *  they always agree on the trigger condition. */
function playerHasAmuletInPlay(state: GameState, cardDb: CardDatabase, playerId: PlayerId): boolean {
  const player = state.players.get(playerId);
  if (!player) return false;
  return player.inPlay.some((c) => cardDb.get(c.definitionKey)?.name === AMULET_OF_OMBOR_NAME);
}

/** True when a Gate to Ombor is already in play on `playerId`'s side. The standard duplicate-relic
 *  block in `isLegalToPlay` is the authoritative gate (owner Q2), but this pre-check keeps the
 *  Talisman offer from surfacing at all in that state -- a cleaner UI signal than "offer, then
 *  refuse at commit." */
function playerHasGateInPlay(state: GameState, cardDb: CardDatabase, playerId: PlayerId): boolean {
  const player = state.players.get(playerId);
  if (!player) return false;
  return player.inPlay.some((c) => cardDb.get(c.definitionKey)?.name === GATE_TO_OMBOR_NAME);
}

registerCardEffect(GATE_TO_OMBOR_NAME, {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (C3 Q2, 2026-08-12 pattern -- see registry.ts's `effectHooks` doc).
  // Guard is the Power block; Talisman covers the "play from hand or deck, ignoring all costs"
  // clause AND the "+1 to Amulet's die rolls" clause. The static region-locked-relic clauses
  // (self-discard if the Magi isn't Underneath; immunity from opposing Relic-discard) live on
  // hooks that Taglat/Gremm's Helmet-style effect-copy would never carry with them, so they are
  // deliberately not enumerated here -- they stay full-card scoped, same as every other card's
  // implicit "static text stays with the printed card" convention.
  effectHooks: {
    Guard: ['deckSearch', 'resolvePower', 'powerTargets'],
    Talisman: ['selfCostOverride', 'offersPlayFromDeck', 'addsToOwnDieRolls'],
  },
  canBeDiscardedFromPlay: () => false,
  onOwnTurnStart: (state, cardDb, self, rng) =>
    applyRegionLockedRelic(state, cardDb, self, (magiDef) => magiDef.regions.includes('Underneath'), rng),
  // Talisman clause 1 (cost side): a TRUE zero when Amulet of Ombor is in play on `self`'s
  // controller side. `selfCostOverride` is the right hook -- `selfCostAdjustment`/`costModifier`
  // would floor at 1 (play.ts's `Math.max(1, ...)`), which doesn't express "ignoring all costs"
  // for a 6-cost Relic. Returns undefined when Amulet isn't in play so normal Relic-cost rules
  // stand (Gate to Ombor's own Guard Power still needs its printed 6 to be paid when the Talisman
  // route isn't active).
  selfCostOverride: (state, cardDb, playerId) =>
    playerHasAmuletInPlay(state, cardDb, playerId) ? 0 : undefined,
  // Talisman clause 1 (from-deck side): expose Gate as playable straight out of its own
  // controller's deck while Amulet is in play. Duplicate-relic block is the standard
  // `isLegalToPlay` check (owner Q2 -- "can't have multiple copies in play on your side"), but
  // we pre-check it here so the offer doesn't surface in that state.
  offersPlayFromDeck: (state, cardDb, self, playerId) => {
    if (self.controllerId !== playerId) return false;
    if (!playerHasAmuletInPlay(state, cardDb, playerId)) return false;
    if (playerHasGateInPlay(state, cardDb, playerId)) return false;
    return true;
  },
  // Talisman clause 2: +1 to every die roll made FOR Amulet of Ombor. `rollingSource` is the
  // luckContext widen from owner Q4 (2026-08-13) -- lets a card-name-scoped bonus be expressed
  // without a bespoke consumer-key hookup. Ignores rolls made for any other source; rolls of 6
  // stay 6 via `rollDie`'s existing `Math.min(sides, raw + bonus)` clamp.
  addsToOwnDieRolls: (_state, cardDb, _self, rollingSource) => {
    const sourceDef = cardDb.get(rollingSource.definitionKey);
    return sourceDef?.name === AMULET_OF_OMBOR_NAME ? 1 : 0;
  },
  deckSearch: {
    count: 1,
    filter: (state, cardDb, playerId, card) => {
      const magi = state.players.get(playerId)?.activeMagi;
      const magiDef = magi ? cardDb.get(magi.definitionKey) : undefined;
      const def = cardDb.get(card.definitionKey);
      return def?.card_type === 'Creature' && !!def.name && (magiDef?.starting?.includes(def.name) ?? false);
    },
  },
  resolvePower: (ctx) => {
    if (ctx.powerName !== 'Guard') return;
    const ids = ctx.chosenDeckSearchIds ?? [];
    if (ids.length !== 1) return;
    const [id] = ids;
    const card = ctx.controllingPlayer.deck.find((c) => c.instanceId === id);
    const def = card ? ctx.cardDb.get(card.definitionKey) : undefined;
    const magi = ctx.controllingPlayer.activeMagi;
    const magiDef = magi ? ctx.cardDb.get(magi.definitionKey) : undefined;
    if (!def || def.card_type !== 'Creature' || !(magiDef?.starting?.includes(def.name) ?? false) || !magi) return;

    const startingEnergy = effectiveStartingEnergy(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, card!);
    const reducedPayment = Math.max(0, startingEnergy - 5);
    if ((magi.currentEnergy ?? 0) < reducedPayment) return;

    magi.currentEnergy = (magi.currentEnergy ?? 0) - reducedPayment;
    const played = playFromZone(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, { owner: ctx.controllingPlayer, zone: 'deck', instanceId: id! }, ctx.controllingPlayer, startingEnergy, ctx.rng);
    if (played) addPermanentTag(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, played, CANNOT_ATTACK);
    shuffleDeck(ctx.controllingPlayer, ctx.rng); // rules-reference.md §12: unconditional reshuffle after a deck search
  },
});
