// Whether a Magi's identity matches a NAME called out in some other card's printed text (e.g.
// Krawg's "If Ashgar is your Magi," Shroud of the Master's "If your Magi is Agram") -- the same
// "a card and its Alternates are the same identity" convention already applied to deck-building
// (deck.ts's magiIdentityNames, used by validateDeck's 3-copy limit and Magi-stack distinctness)
// and starting-card tutoring (setup.ts's impliedStartingCardNames/alternateStartingCardNames),
// just extended to card-EFFECT text. Confirmed with the project owner (2026-07-10): any card
// whose text names a specific Magi should also match that Magi's Alternates.
//
// CORRECTED 2026-07-25 (project owner, re-reading Shadow Empress's printed text). This module used
// to layer a static `EFFECT_ONLY_ALIASES` table (Shadow Empress -> Agram) directly into
// `magiCountsAs`, making the alias GLOBAL and PERMANENT. Both were wrong, and they are wrong in
// different ways -- the distinction is worth stating precisely, because Shadow Empress has TWO
// separate identity relationships that are easy to conflate:
//
//   1. Shadow Empress IS a true Alternate of WARRADA -- a real database `alternate` field. Like
//      every Alternate, that is intrinsic and unconditional: it holds in every context, it can
//      never be locked down or removed, and it constrains deck-building. Handled entirely by
//      `magiIdentityNames` below; nothing in this file is needed for it.
//   2. Shadow Empress merely COUNTS AS Agram, and only because her Mastery of Shadows EFFECT says
//      so: "Shadow Empress may play Spells as though she were Agram and your Spells in play treat
//      her as though she were Agram." That is narrower than an Alternate in two ways a static
//      table cannot express -- it applies to SPELLS ONLY (not to Relics such as Shroud of the
//      Master, Agram's Staff, or Agram's Plaything), and being an Effect it STOPS APPLYING the
//      moment that Effect is locked down (Rayje's Belt's definition-level lock, Feet of Stone's
//      instance-level EFFECTS_LOCKED_DOWN tag).
//
// So the Agram alias now lives behind `magiCountsAsForSpell`, which callers must opt into and which
// re-checks lockdown every call. Plain `magiCountsAs` is once again purely database-driven.
// This module is deliberately NOT imported by deck.ts or setup.ts -- keep those purely
// database-driven (and note that even the Spell-scoped alias must never reach them: it is an
// in-game effect, not a deck-legality fact).

import type { CardDatabase } from '../types/card.js';
import type { CardInstance } from '../types/instance.js';
import type { GameState } from '../types/state.js';
import { magiIdentityNames } from '../deck.js';
import { isCardEffectLockedDown } from '../lockdown.js';

/**
 * "Counts as" rulings granted by a Magi's own EFFECT text and scoped to SPELLS specifically, with
 * no database `alternate` link. Consulted only by `magiCountsAsForSpell`, and only while the
 * granting Magi's Effects are live.
 *
 * Currently just Shadow Empress -> Agram (Mastery of Shadows). Her real, unconditional Alternate
 * relationship is with Warrada and is database-driven -- deliberately NOT listed here.
 */
const SPELL_SCOPED_EFFECT_ALIASES: Readonly<Record<string, readonly string[]>> = {
  'Shadow Empress': ['Agram'],
};

/**
 * True if `magi`'s INTRINSIC card identity -- its own name or its database Alternates -- matches
 * `name`. Unconditional: no lockdown check, because an Alternate relationship is a property of the
 * card itself and nothing in the game can suppress it.
 *
 * This is the right check for the overwhelming majority of "if your Magi is <X>" text. Use
 * `magiCountsAsForSpell` INSTEAD only where the effect being resolved is a Spell (or the play of
 * one) -- see that function.
 */
export function magiCountsAs(cardDb: CardDatabase, magi: CardInstance, name: string): boolean {
  const def = cardDb.get(magi.definitionKey);
  if (!def) return false;
  return magiIdentityNames(def).includes(name);
}

/**
 * `magiCountsAs`, plus any Spell-scoped effect-granted alias that is currently active.
 *
 * Call this ONLY from a Spell context: a Spell resolving, a Spell already in play reading the
 * controller's Magi identity, or the legality check for PLAYING a Spell. Everything else -- Relic
 * Powers/Effects, Creature text, Magi-reveal handling, deck-building -- must use plain
 * `magiCountsAs`, or Shadow Empress will wrongly satisfy "if your Magi is Agram" on cards her
 * printed text does not cover.
 *
 * The lockdown re-check is the point of taking `state`: unlike an Alternate, an effect-granted
 * identity is only as durable as the Effect granting it.
 */
export function magiCountsAsForSpell(
  state: GameState,
  cardDb: CardDatabase,
  magi: CardInstance,
  name: string
): boolean {
  if (magiCountsAs(cardDb, magi, name)) return true;
  const def = cardDb.get(magi.definitionKey);
  if (!def) return false;
  if (!(SPELL_SCOPED_EFFECT_ALIASES[def.name] ?? []).includes(name)) return false;
  return !isCardEffectLockedDown(state, cardDb, magi);
}
