// Crystal Parmalag -- "Anti-Magic": two clauses.
//   "Crystal Parmalag is not affected by opposing Spells, Powers or Effects that specifically
//   discard Creatures from play." -- registry.ts's canBeDiscardedFromPlay, exact same shape as
//   Kybar's Fang/Gift of the Weave/Gate to Ombor -- a pure, zero-new-plumbing implementation
//   already covered by an existing hook.
//
//   "Your Spells, Powers, and Effects may not prevent Crystal Parmalag from losing energy." Built
//   2026-08-13 (deferred-list full re-audit, Underneath region pass, Bucket B). Prior header
//   claimed "no real card currently grants a broadcast loss-reduction to other own Creatures, so
//   this clause has no observable effect today" -- STALE. Task #29 (2026-07-15) shipped
//   `grantsOpposingEnergyLossReductionTo` and Arderian-Guard Wings' Feathered Protection uses it
//   to broadcast a 2-energy Spell/Power reduction to every one of its controller's Creatures;
//   task #45 (2026-07-18) shipped `grantsAttackLossReductionTo` and Pruitt, Ringsmith's Nurture
//   uses it for combat losses. Both would otherwise apply to Crystal Parmalag when it shares its
//   controller's board, and this clause is the exact anti-protection that says they must NOT.
//
//   Built via registry.ts's `suppressesProtectionFrom` (task #552, 2026-07-27: Cawh's Fearsome,
//   Tunnel Parmalag's Shield). Scoped narrower than Cawh: "YOUR Spells, Powers, and Effects" is
//   controller-only ("Your"), not "Other cards" -- an opposing Wings-like broadcast would still
//   reduce Crystal Parmalag's loss (there is no real card doing that today, but the scope belongs
//   in the card, not in the hook). Kinds covered are 'energyLoss' and 'combatEnergyLoss' -- both
//   directions of loss the printed "losing energy" covers -- but NOT 'specificDiscard' (a
//   different mechanism, and Crystal Parmalag's clause 1 already handles that separately).
//
//   THE SELF-EXEMPTION is defensive rather than load-bearing on this card: Crystal Parmalag's own
//   clause 1 is discard immunity, not a loss-prevention, so it wouldn't be canceled by clause 2
//   even without the check. But every implementer of `suppressesProtectionFrom` follows the same
//   `protector.instanceId !== self.instanceId` convention (see the family's registry.ts doc
//   comment); keeping the check here means a future addition to Crystal Parmalag's own kit that
//   IS loss-reducing won't silently cancel itself.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Crystal Parmalag', {
  canBeDiscardedFromPlay: () => false,
  suppressesProtectionFrom: (state, cardDb, self, protector, kind) => {
    if (protector.instanceId === self.instanceId) return false; // family convention (see header)
    if (protector.controllerId !== self.controllerId) return false; // "YOUR Spells, Powers, and Effects"
    return kind === 'energyLoss' || kind === 'combatEnergyLoss'; // "losing energy" -- both routes, NOT specificDiscard
  },
});
