// Rayje's Cloak (Universal Relic, cost 2) -- unnamed Effect: "Opposing cards neither prevent your
// Creatures from attacking nor prevent opposing cards from defending. Opposing cards do not
// prevent your cards from using their Powers and Effects."
//
// DOC-ONLY FILE. There is no hook to register: the Cloak is a passive that other code consults,
// exactly like ashio.ts. Its whole implementation is the shared "is this restriction still in
// force?" layer in restrictions.ts, which every restriction read site now goes through:
//
//   * "prevent your Creatures from attacking"  -> combat.ts's isLegalAttack, via isRestrictionActive
//                                                 (CANNOT_ATTACK)
//   * "prevent opposing cards from defending"  -> combat.ts's two defender checks, via
//                                                 isRestrictionActive (CANNOT_BE_ATTACKED)
//   * "using their Powers"                     -> power.ts, via isRestrictionActive
//                                                 (CANNOT_USE_POWER) AND the blocksPowerUse
//                                                 broadcast, which skips opposing blockers
//   * "using their ... Effects"                -> lockdown.ts's isCardEffectLockedDown, the single
//                                                 choke point every effect-hook dispatch site uses
//
// All four reduce to the same rule -- a restriction is cancelled when the player who caused it is
// not the Cloak's controller -- so there is deliberately no per-clause logic anywhere. See
// restrictions.ts for the full write-up, including why self-imposed restrictions (Baby Hyren,
// Ascend, Blygt, Chelon) must survive and why the Cloak is treated as protecting itself from
// Rayje's Belt.
//
// Registered here purely so `isCardImplemented` reports the Cloak as built and it stops showing up
// in unregistered-card audits.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect("Rayje's Cloak", {});
