// Equilibrate (Universal Spell, cost 3) -- "All Creatures in play with more than their starting
// energy are reduced to their starting energy."
//
// Weave + Universal Spell pass, Category A (2026-07-27).
//
// OWNER RULING 2026-07-27: this is a HARD SET, not an energy loss, and it is one-directional --
// only Creatures ABOVE their starting energy are touched, and it never restores one that is below.
// That ruling is what makes this a direct `currentEnergy` write rather than a `discardEnergy` call,
// and the distinction is deliberate and load-bearing:
//   - No reduction hooks fire. Weave Hut, Rayje's Sword, Baby Furok and the rest of the
//     energy-loss-reduction family do not blunt it, because no energy is "lost".
//   - No `onBeforeEnergyRemoved` / CONDEMNED / Sunburn amplification. Same reason.
// If a future ruling reverses this into a real loss, the change is to route through `discardEnergy`
// with the per-Creature excess as the amount -- not to add hooks here.
//
// `checkCreatureDefeats` IS still required, and the reason is easy to get wrong: a Creature's
// printed starting energy is its COST (see targeting.ts's `printedStartingEnergy`), and the
// database has genuine ZERO-cost Creatures -- Cloud Orshaa, Cyclone Xyx's cheaper cousins, 724
// Creatures carry `starting: null` and take their starting energy from `cost` instead. A 0-cost
// Creature sitting above 0 therefore gets set TO 0 by this Spell, which by the Comprehensive
// Rules ("a Creature is considered defeated when it is reduced to zero energy") defeats it. An
// earlier draft of this file asserted the floor was "always > 0" and skipped the check; that was
// simply false, and a test using a 0-cost fixture Creature is what exposed it.
//
// Every Creature in play on BOTH sides ("All Creatures in play", no qualifier).
// `printedStartingEnergy` rather than `def.starting` so per-instance starting-energy overrides
// (Slime Stone and its family) are honored.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { allCreaturesInPlay, effectiveStartingEnergy } from '../targeting.js';
import { checkCreatureDefeats } from '../energy.js';

registerCardEffect('Equilibrate', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    for (const creature of allCreaturesInPlay(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb)) {
      const cap = effectiveStartingEnergy(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, creature);
      if ((creature.currentEnergy ?? 0) > cap) creature.currentEnergy = cap;
    }
    checkCreatureDefeats(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb);
  },
});
