// Lascinth -- "Weave" is built: "Whenever Lascinth attacks or is attacked, before energy is
// removed, you may move one energy between it and one of your other Weave Creatures in play."
// (see weave.ts).
//
// "Reflexes: Whenever Lascinth is attacked, it removes energy immediately, before Creatures
// normally remove energy." Built 2026-07-28 -- the DEFENDER-side mirror of Stealth/Seaweed
// Lascinth, on combat.ts's step-7 first-strike slot (see CombatContext.firstStrike's doc comment).
// Unlike those two it is a permanent printed Effect, not a Spell or a paid Power, so there is no
// tag and no turn scope at all: if Lascinth is the defender, it strikes first, always.
//
// The old deferral note here read "breaks the simultaneous-damage assumption," and it was pointing
// straight at the real bug -- that assumption was ALSO being broken, silently and wrongly, by the
// Stealth build that shipped first. Reflexes is a true first strike (RT 11/12/01, quoted about this
// exact card): "If Lascinth removes all the opponent's energy as a result of this early shot, then
// the creature immediately dies before getting the chance to do its own damage in return." The
// kill-suppresses-return-damage half lives in combat.ts's step-7 block, so it is shared by all
// three first-strike cards rather than re-implemented here. If the early shot does NOT kill, the
// attacker still removes its full step-6 energy and Lascinth takes the whole blow -- the early
// strike bought nothing.
// "Hunger: Lascinth must attack each turn, if able." is built (task #44 Part B, 2026-07-18,
// must-attack enforcement architecture) -- same standing self-obligation shape as Garan/
// Junjertrug: `onOwnTurnStart` re-tags every turn.
//
// "Your cards may not prevent Lascinth from attacking" (Hunger's SECOND sentence) is built too as
// of task #715 (2026-08-11, Category C deferred-gap closure pass) via the new attacker-side hook
// `preventsOwnControllerAttackPrevention`. combat.ts's `isLegalAttack` reads this once at the top
// of the attack-prevention section and, when true, treats own-controller-sourced preventions as
// absent at each of five gates: the CANNOT_ATTACK tag scan (via `isRestrictionActive`'s optional
// source-filter set), the Crystallize attached-scan, the `preventsAttackAndPowerUseSameTurn`
// broadcast (Archid's Stunning), the `preventsAttackOf` broadcast (Paranoia), and the
// `preventsHolderAttack` attached scan (Entrench). Opposing-source preventions still work
// unchanged (Rayje's Cloak is the mechanism for THOSE, untouched); sourceless printed self-
// restrictions still stand (they are the card's own characteristic, not "your cards" preventing
// anything). Narrow by design -- only Lascinth registers this hook.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { applyWeave } from './weave.js';
import { addDurationTag, MUST_ATTACK_THIS_TURN } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Lascinth', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (C3 Q2, 2026-08-12: Taglat). Reflexes is the defender-side first-
  // strike arming on `onAttack`; Hunger is the per-turn must-attack retag plus its own second
  // sentence ("your cards may not prevent Lascinth from attacking"); Weave is the move hook +
  // `weaveConfig`.
  effectHooks: {
    Reflexes: ['onAttack'],
    Hunger: ['onOwnTurnStart', 'preventsOwnControllerAttackPrevention'],
    Weave: ['weaveConfig', 'onBeforeEnergyRemoved'],
  },
  weaveConfig: { eligibleRegions: ['Weave'], mode: 'both' },
  onBeforeEnergyRemoved: (ctx, self) => applyWeave(ctx, self, ['Weave']),
  onAttack: (ctx, self) => {
    if (ctx.defender?.instanceId !== self.instanceId) return;
    ctx.firstStrike = 'defender';
  },
  onOwnTurnStart: (state, cardDb, self) => {
    addDurationTag(state, cardDb, self, MUST_ATTACK_THIS_TURN, state.turnNumber);
  },
  preventsOwnControllerAttackPrevention: () => true,
});
