// Drajan -- two printed Effects:
//
// FIGHT: "Opposing Powers cost one additional energy to use." Built via registry.ts's
// `powerCostModifier`. Powers have a single choke point (`usePower`); this is the standard
// gate for that hook.
//
// FAIR: "Other players' cards do not use Effects during attacks." RESOLVED 2026-08-13 (Wave C3
// of the deferred-list re-audit).
//
// Mechanism: `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive`, consulted from
// `filterOwnEffectForLockdown` -- the same single choke point Sorreah's Effects half and Rayje's
// Belt's Lockdown already go through. When Drajan is any player's active Magi AND the game is
// currently inside an attack step (`state.currentAction?.source === 'combat'`, set by
// `combat.ts#declareAttack` for the entire span onBeforeEnergyRemoved through afterCombat, then
// restored), every OPPOSING-controlled card's named printed Effects are treated as if they were
// Rayje-locked: fine-grained per-Effect-hook stripping if the target declares `effectHooks`,
// coarse whole-card silence otherwise (identical fallback to how Rayje's Belt degrades).
//
// Drajan's own Fair can itself be Rayje-Belt-locked (naming "Fair"); when locked, the external
// gate skips Drajan as a suppressor and Fight continues to work (Fight has its own separate
// `effectHooks` entry pointing at `powerCostModifier`, so a Rayje-lock of Fair does not
// collaterally silence Fight -- the per-Effect narrowing lets each half be locked independently).
//
// Owner Q&A that shaped this closure (all 2026-08-13):
//   Q1 (what "Effects" means): anything with printed "Effect - " prefix -- an entry with a `name`
//       in the card's `effects[]` array. See `sorreah.ts`'s header for the traps
//       (Spell-granted vs. Effect-granted origin, Reflexes vs. Stealth).
//   Q2 (scope): all "Effect -" hooks that fire during the combat attack step's stages -- gated
//       by `state.currentAction?.source === 'combat'`, which covers the full declareAttack span.
//   Q3 (other players' cards): opposing player only (1v1 game). Drajan's own field is unaffected.
//   Q4 (afterCombat): YES, afterCombat is part of the 8 stages of the attack step per the rules
//       and is inside `state.currentAction.source === 'combat'`, so it IS suppressed.
//   Q5 (mid-attack Drajan reveal): YES, applies from that moment on. The check is live at each
//       broadcast (`externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive` re-scans each call), not pre-cached at
//       attack start -- so if Drajan is revealed as the active Magi mid-attack (e.g. by a Magi-
//       swap Power or a Magi-defeat mid-combat that reveals the next one), the suppression
//       applies to every subsequent broadcast in the same attack.
//   Q6 (Sorreah joint scope): Sorreah's Effects half shares the same origin-detection primitive
//       and lives in the same helper -- see `sorreah.ts`'s own header.
//
// Shares infrastructure with Sorreah's Suppress -- see `sorreah.ts`'s header and
// `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive` for the shared primitive.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Drajan', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (C3 Q2, 2026-08-12: Taglat). Fight's `powerCostModifier` is its
  // only local hook. Fair's Effects-suppression is enforced externally by
  // `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive` (no local hook to list here); the
  // empty array documents Fair as a known printed Effect on this card so a Rayje-lock of "Fair"
  // gets the fine-grained per-name path (strips nothing local, and the external gate handles
  // itself via the same lockdown-name check), leaving Fight intact rather than collaterally
  // silencing the whole card via the coarse fallback.
  effectHooks: {
    Fight: ['powerCostModifier'],
    Fair: [],
  },
  powerCostModifier: (state, cardDb, powerUserId, sourceDef, self) => (powerUserId !== self.controllerId ? 1 : 0),
});
