// Yaki -- "Double Strike: Each of your Creatures may attack twice each turn."
//
// A STANDING grant (registry.ts's grantsBonusAttacksTo), not a one-shot sweep. This used to loop
// creaturesControlledBy in onOwnTurnStart and write the extra-attack counter on each Creature,
// which read fine but meant "each of your Creatures" really meant "each of your Creatures as of the
// start of your turn". Task #557, playtest 2026-07-27: the tester flipped Yaki up and used
// Warrior's Boots to bring a Furok in mid-turn -- the Furok had not existed when the sweep ran, so
// it only ever got Yaki's Gauntlets' charge and attacked twice instead of three times. Diagnosed at
// first as a stacking/math bug; it was a sequencing one. Asking the grant live at each attack
// declaration makes arrival order irrelevant.
//
// No "may attack twice" wording is checked against a per-turn budget here -- durationTags.ts's
// effectiveBonusAttacks sums this with any one-shot grants, and combat.ts compares the total against
// attacksThisTurn.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Yaki', {
  grantsBonusAttacksTo: (state, cardDb, self, target) =>
    target.controllerId === self.controllerId && cardDb.get(target.definitionKey)?.card_type === 'Creature' ? 1 : undefined,
});
