// Valkan -- "Pyromancy: Whenever Valkan plays a Spell that discards energy from any number of
// Creatures, discard two additional energy from each of those Creatures." Near-identical shape to
// Scroll of Fire's own Pyromancy (task #51, 2026-07-20), reusing the same
// onOwnPowerDiscardedOpposingEnergyFromCreature broadcast, but: Spell-only (no Power half in the
// printed text, unlike Scroll of Fire/Amanax), and +2 instead of +1.
//
// No separate "is my Magi Valkan" identity check is needed (unlike tithragar.ts/
// ulligsSlingshot.ts's magiCountsAs, which check a THIRD-PARTY card's printed reference to some
// other named Magi) -- this ability is registered directly on Valkan's OWN card, and the
// broadcast this hook rides only ever calls a contributor's registered effect when that exact
// contributor is on the acting (casting) player's own board. Valkan is a Magi, so the only way
// its own hook can fire at all is if Valkan IS that player's active Magi already -- there's no
// "Valkan sitting unrevealed in the Magi queue" case to exclude, since queue members are never
// broadcast contributors.
//
// "any number of Creatures" (not "opposing Creatures") is broader in principle than every other
// card in this family, all of which are built against the opposing-only energy-diff broadcast --
// but every real Cald Spell that discards Creature energy targets an OPPOSING Creature (removing
// your own Creature's energy would be self-defeating), so this is a documented simplification with
// no live card difference, consistent with how Scroll of Fire/Amanax/Ithapher already interpret
// their own "Spells or Powers" text through this same opposing-only hook.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { discardEnergy } from '../effects.js';

registerCardEffect('Valkan', {
  onOwnPowerDiscardedOpposingEnergyFromCreature: (state, cardDb, self, sourceCard, target) => {
    if (cardDb.get(sourceCard.definitionKey)?.card_type !== 'Spell') return; // Spell-only, no Power half
    discardEnergy(state, cardDb, target, 2, 'spell');
  },
});
