// Marella (Weave Magi) -- "Vapid: Marella may only draw one card total each turn." Built in the
// Weave region pass #49, Category B.
//
// Implemented via capsDrawCountAt (Reality Anchor precedent, task #50k) scoped to Marella's OWN
// controller's Draw Step: return a cap of 1 only when Marella's controller is the active (drawing)
// player, undefined otherwise, so it never limits the opponent's draws (Vapid restricts Marella
// only, unlike Reality Anchor's both-players cap).
//
// KNOWN SIMPLIFICATION: capsDrawCountAt only gates the Draw Step (turn.ts's runDrawPhase). The
// literal "one card TOTAL each turn" would also block extra draws from a Power/Effect after the
// first -- that needs a per-turn cross-source draw counter this engine doesn't have yet. The Draw
// Step is where essentially all draws happen, and the uncovered case only makes Marella's own
// downside slightly more lenient (never helps the opponent), so it's left as a documented gap.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Marella', {
  capsDrawCountAt: (state, _cardDb, self) => (state.activePlayerId === self.controllerId ? 1 : undefined),
});
