// Riptide (Spell, Orothe, cost 2) -- four printed clauses:
//   1. "All players discard all but four cards from their hand." BUILT 2026-08-11 (post-audit
//      deferred-gap closure pass, Category C), via a new generalization of Mudslide's
//      `pendingBoardSacrificeSequence` shape: `pendingSequentialZonePick` (types/state.ts), a
//      single bounded multi-select instead of two fixed single picks -- exactly the "each player
//      picks which of their own hand cards to discard down to N" mechanism this comment used to
//      say didn't exist yet. See that field's own doc comment and play.ts's
//      `previewSequentialZonePickFor`/`resolveSequentialZonePickFor`; Horn of Renewal is the
//      shape's other user. WHICH cards to keep is each player's own choice (Elios' Dream Hard
//      "discard down to N" precedent) -- the COUNT discarded is fixed by hand size, not chosen.
//   2. "Until the end of your next turn, all other Spells, Powers, or Effects that cause opponents
//      to discard cards from their hand may not be played or used." BUILT 2026-08-11 (post-audit
//      deferred-gap closure pass, Category D, task #718). Owner ruling: the ban is SELF-scoped to
//      the Riptide caster -- Player 1 casts Riptide → Player 1's own hand-discard cards can't be
//      played/used through end of Player 1's next turn; Player 2's hand-discard cards continue to
//      work normally. Mechanism: `PlayerState.riptideBanExpiresAfterTurnNumber` (types/state.ts)
//      stamped here to `nextOwnTurnNumber(state)` on the caster; a new declarative-static
//      `causesOpponentHandDiscard` registry tag (~15 tagged cards) identifies affected
//      Spells/Powers/Effects; three gates read the ban: `play.ts#isLegalToPlay`,
//      `power.ts#isLegalPowerUse`, and inside the ~3 Effect-shaped tagged cards' own hook bodies
//      (Adis, Weethan, Zaya). See `causesOpponentHandDiscard`'s doc comment in registry.ts for
//      the full mechanism writeup and the audit inventory.
//   3. "Opposing cards may not discard Riptide from your hand." BUILT -- registry.ts's new
//      preventsOwnDiscardFromHand hook (self-only, narrower than blocksHostileHandDiscard's
//      all-or-nothing player-wide block).
//   4. "Orothe Shadow Magi may play Riptide." Needs no code -- shadow_play is data-driven
//      (regions.ts).
//
// NOTE: the source data originally scraped this card's first clause as "...from their LANDS" --
// Magi-Nation has no "lands" zone; corrected at the source (cards_final.json) to "hand," per the
// project owner (2026-07-24), before this file was written.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { getOpponents } from '../types/state.js';
import { nextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Riptide', {
  preventsOwnDiscardFromHand: () => true,
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    const casterId = ctx.controllingPlayer.playerId;
    const opponent = getOpponents(ctx.state, casterId)[0];
    // Clause 1: per-player hand-discard-down-to-4 sequence.
    ctx.state.pendingSequentialZonePick = {
      remainingPlayerIds: opponent ? [casterId, opponent.playerId] : [casterId],
      sourceInstanceId: ctx.source.instanceId,
      kind: 'riptideHandDiscard',
    };
    // Clause 2: self-scoped ban on the caster's own subsequent hand-discard cards until end of
    // their own next turn. "next own turn" is the same duration wording every other same-shaped
    // "until end of your next turn" tag uses, computed the same way (nextOwnTurnNumber factors in
    // whether the current turn is already this player's).
    ctx.controllingPlayer.riptideBanExpiresAfterTurnNumber = nextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
  },
});
