// Sneak Attack (Spell, Bograth/Paradwyn) -- "Until the beginning of your next turn, whenever a
// Creature attacks or is attacked, you may choose to have either or both Creatures remove energy
// equal to their starting energy instead of their current energy. Energy removed in attacks
// cannot be reduced or prevented." Bograth Spell pass, Category C (2026-07-20) -- see
// docs/plans/bograth-spell-pass-plan.md for the full scoping writeup (this was originally scoped
// as a "hard, deferred" case until the project owner flagged Kioko's Motivate/Demotivate as the
// exact precedent for the substitution logic).
//
// resolveSpell just arms PlayerState.sneakAttackUntilTurn (beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber -- the
// printed wording is "until the beginning," not "until the end," matching Lurking Minani/Jungle
// Jile/Snag Hyren's identical phrasing); the actual per-attack substitution and the "cannot be
// reduced or prevented" rule both live in combat.ts/durationTags.ts, checked generically since
// this Spell has no in-play card to hang a duration tag on by the time a future combat happens
// (same reasoning as lightningSand.ts's own player-level charge field). See combat.ts's own
// "Sneak Attack" comment (right after the onAttack broadcast loop) for the substitution itself.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Sneak Attack', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.controllingPlayer.sneakAttackUntilTurn = beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
  },
});
