// Korrit + Giant Korrit -- "Pack Hunt: Instead of its normal attack, [this Creature] can attack WITH
// one of your other Creatures. Both [this Creature] and the attacking Creature remove energy from the
// defending Creature, but [this Creature] loses no energy in the attack." Built task #48, 2026-07-18,
// the Underneath region pass -- Category C, the co-attacker combat mechanism.
//
// The whole mechanism lives in combat.ts (AttackDeclaration.coAttackerInstanceId +
// CombatContext.coAttacker): when the UI declares a Pack Hunt, isLegalAttack checks this card's
// `canPackHunt` and that the co-attacker is a legal attacker in its own right; declareAttack makes
// this Korrit immune to the defender's counter-damage, has the co-attacker also hit the defender and
// take the counter, and marks both as having attacked. So the card itself just declares eligibility.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Korrit', {
  canPackHunt: () => true,
});

registerCardEffect('Giant Korrit', {
  canPackHunt: () => true,
});
