// Intensify (Universal Spell, cost 1) -- "The next Spell or Power that discards energy from one or
// more Magi instead discards twice as much energy from each of those Magi."
//
// Weave + Universal Spell pass, Category C (2026-07-27).
//
// NOT scoped to its caster. The printed text says "the next Spell or Power," with no "your" -- an
// opponent's Spell arms into it just as readily, which is the whole double-edge of the card. Hence
// GameState.pendingIntensify rather than a PlayerState field; see that field's doc comment for the
// `used`-flag design and why the window is consumed at the end of a resolution rather than on the
// first Magi hit.
//
// The doubling itself lives in effects.ts's `discardEnergy`, applied to the BASE amount before every
// reduction, cap and block -- "instead discards twice as much" replaces what the Spell removes
// rather than adding a second, separate hit. So a Magi that is fully protected still loses nothing,
// and a -2 reduction subtracts 2 from the doubled figure rather than from the original.
//
// Intensify does not consume itself: its own resolution discards no Magi energy, so `used` is still
// false when play.ts reaches the resolution boundary and the window survives to the NEXT Spell.
//
// A second Intensify played while one is already armed is a no-op rather than a x4 stack -- the
// printed text describes one replacement effect on one Spell, not a multiplier that composes.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Intensify', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.state.pendingIntensify = { used: false };
  },
});
