// Creeping Chill (Spell, Bograth/Kybar's Teeth) -- "Until the end of your next turn, whenever one
// of your Kybar's Teeth Creatures is attacked, it gains three energy for each of your Bograth
// Creatures in play, and whenever one of your Bograth Creatures attacks, it gains three energy
// for each of your Kybar's Teeth Creatures in play." Bograth Spell pass, Category C (2026-07-20)
// -- see docs/plans/bograth-spell-pass-plan.md for the full scoping writeup. ushi.ts's own
// comment flagged the nearest analog (Motivate: "each Creature with the Weave Effect gains two
// energy as it attacks") as deferred for needing "a temporary broadcast grant with its own
// stored-modifier tracking" -- this is that mechanism, though built narrowly for this card rather
// than generalized to Motivate's own different trigger shape (Weave-Effect-tagged, not
// region-count-scaled); revisit Motivate separately if it turns out to fit the same shape.
//
// resolveSpell just arms PlayerState.creepingChillUntilTurn (nextOwnTurnNumber -- "until the END
// of your next turn," the more common wording, distinct from Sneak Attack's "until the
// BEGINNING"). The actual energy gain lives in combat.ts, applied BEFORE the ctx.locked snapshot
// (same timing onBeforeEnergyRemoved hooks use) so it's real, not just a locked-combat-math
// adjustment -- see combat.ts's own "Creeping Chill" comment (right before "Step 3: snapshot").

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { nextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Creeping Chill', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.controllingPlayer.creepingChillUntilTurn = nextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
  },
});
