// Rock Hyren -- "Invulnerability: Rock Hyren loses two less energy in attacks and from opposing
// Spells, Powers, and Effects. Your Spells, Powers, and other Effects may not prevent Rock Hyren
// from losing energy."
//
// Both halves are built:
//   - "-2 in attacks" is applyInvulnerability (combat.ts's own locked-energy math), same as every
//     other Kybar's Teeth Invulnerability card.
//   - "-2 from opposing Spells, Powers, and Effects" is registry.ts's new
//     opposingEnergyLossReduction hook, consulted by effects.ts's discardEnergy for BOTH `cause`
//     values (unlike Shifty, which is 'effect'-only) -- Rock Hyren's own text has no such split.
//   - "Your Spells, Powers, and other Effects may not prevent Rock Hyren from losing energy":
//     confirmed with the project owner 2026-07-11 -- this is an ANTI-STACKING clause aimed at the
//     controller's OWN protective effects, not the opponent's. Two concrete examples given: Targ'n's
//     Enhanced Invulnerability (+1 more reduction for creatures that PRINT the Invulnerability
//     effect) must NOT apply on top of Rock Hyren's own -2, and a hypothetical Burrow grant would
//     not add Burrow's cap on top either. Implemented as a hardcoded name check at each of the (two)
//     real stacking sources rather than a shared mechanism, since Rock Hyren is the only card with
//     this clause: targN.ts excludes Rock Hyren from Enhanced Invulnerability, and
//     shardOfTheGreatFossil.ts excludes it from Shield (which would otherwise grant Rock Hyren total
//     attack immunity, also a form of "preventing it from losing energy"). Burrow itself can never
//     reach Rock Hyren today -- both burrow-granting cards (Muggum, Strag's Ring) restrict their
//     target pool to Bograth/Underneath Creatures, and Rock Hyren is Kybar's Teeth only -- so no
//     code change was needed there, just this note for if that ever changes.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { applyInvulnerability } from './invulnerability.js';

registerCardEffect('Rock Hyren', {
  onAttack: (ctx, self) => applyInvulnerability(ctx, self, 2),
  opposingEnergyLossReduction: () => 2,
});
