// Swirling Orshaa -- "As you play Swirling Orshaa, reduce its cost by three. Swirling Orshaa is
// not considered to be in play when checking to see if your Magi is defeated, and it cannot
// attack Magi directly." -- post-playtest correctness pass, P1 (2026-07-12), via the shared
// illusionCreature.ts helper.
//
// "Morph" ("as another Spell, Power, or Effect references a specific Creature type or region, you
// may have Swirling Orshaa be considered that specific Creature type or region until the end of
// the turn") -- built 2026-07-24 (Spell-pass audit follow-up) on the Checkpoint B-derived
// identityOverride mechanism. Covers the Power/Spell half only: registry.ts's
// offersIdentityOverrideBeforeChoices fires from power.ts/play.ts BEFORE that ability's own
// target-picker opens, over BOTH players' boards (matching Checkpoint B's own region-swap
// broadcast), whenever the triggering ability declared a nonzero specifiedRegions or
// specifiedCreatureTypes -- Orshaa accepts any offer unconditionally (no cost, no restriction),
// since its own printed text has neither. resolveIdentityOverride writes a PERSISTENT
// self.identityOverride (unlike a region-swap's call-scoped state.activeRegionSwap), expiring at
// the end of THIS turn per the field's own "present through that turn" sweep semantics.
//
// The "Effect" half of the printed text (reacting to a CONTINUOUS check like Braggle's Mirror
// Shield or Sarazen Outcast's Bane, which have no discrete target-picker moment for Checkpoint B
// to intercept) is a separate, later architecture project -- deliberately out of scope for this
// hook, not silently dropped. See docs/deferred-card-mechanics.md.
//
// BUCKET D re-confirmed (deferred-list re-audit, 2026-08-13). Verified against current infra:
// `offersIdentityOverrideBeforeChoices` (this file, plus power.ts:1653/combat.ts:2201/
// play.ts:1653) only fires from three call sites, ALL guarded on a discrete "an ability just
// declared specifiedRegions/specifiedCreatureTypes" moment. Continuous-check readers of a
// Creature's identity (Braggle's Mirror Shield's per-attack region equality check, Sarazen
// Outcast's Bane's per-tick type check, and every effectiveRegions/matchesCreatureFamily call in
// the passive-broadcast paths -- targeting.ts, combat.ts's damage-modifier reads, lockdown.ts,
// etc.) never open a "would you like to be X right now?" window. Missing primitive: a
// **reactive identity-override broadcast at continuous-check time**, symmetric to how
// `preventsRegionSwapForFiltering` guards region-swap reads but for a per-check Orshaa opt-in.
// Not a one-file build: it would need to piggyback on every effectiveRegions/matchesCreatureFamily
// caller (~40+ sites) OR a wrapper helper that snapshots-then-restores identityOverride around
// each continuous read, plus a "did any check just fire?" pending-choice queue for the "may" --
// none of which exist today. Defer to a dedicated architecture session.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { applyIllusionEntry } from './illusionCreature.js';

registerCardEffect('Swirling Orshaa', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (C3 Q2, 2026-08-12: Taglat). Only Morph is mapped; the second
  // (unnamed) Illusion clause -- selfCostAdjustment + its onPlay applyIllusionEntry -- has
  // no name to key on and falls through to whole-card grant.
  effectHooks: {
    Morph: ['offersIdentityOverrideBeforeChoices', 'resolveIdentityOverride'],
  },
  selfCostAdjustment: () => -3,
  onPlay: (state, cardDb, played, self) => {
    if (played.instanceId === self.instanceId) applyIllusionEntry(state, cardDb, self);
  },
  offersIdentityOverrideBeforeChoices: (
    state,
    cardDb,
    self,
    actorPlayerId,
    abilityKind,
    sourceDef,
    sourceInstanceId,
    specifiedRegions,
    specifiedCreatureTypes
  ) => specifiedRegions.length > 0 || specifiedCreatureTypes.length > 0,
  resolveIdentityOverride: (state, cardDb, self, kind, value, expiresAfterTurnNumber) => {
    self.identityOverride = { kind, value, expiresAfterTurnNumber };
  },
});
