// Korg & Zet -- Double Magi (counts as two Magi for deck construction, same "Double Magi detector"
// class as The Dark Twins). Two printed Effects:
//   "Korg: Korg & Zet may play no more than two cards each turn and may not play Relics." BOTH
//   halves now built.
//     - "may not play Relics" via registry.ts's `restrictsOwnPlayOf` (same mechanism as All-High
//       King Korg's Super Clever and Korg's own Dis...ray).
//     - "no more than two cards each turn" via the new `restrictsOwnPlayCountAt` hook +
//       `PlayerState.cardsPlayedThisTurn` counter (Bucket D Batch B closure 2026-08-13). Counter
//       increments in play.ts#playCard AND effects.ts#playFromZone (the two disjoint entry points
//       for a card entering play from outside play), resets for EVERY player at every turn
//       boundary in turn.ts#runStartOfTurnHooks. Owner Q&A 2026-08-13:
//         Q1 -- All plays count (Creatures, Spells, Relics). A Spell that plays another card
//               as part of its resolution counts BOTH (the Spell itself + the nested play). If
//               the cap is hit mid-Spell-resolution, the nested play's isLegalToPlay refuses
//               ("the spell is played, but they can no longer play the thing the spell was
//               targeting, and so the play fizzles"). Fizzle+shuffle behavior on deck-searches
//               is the caller's responsibility; isLegalToPlay just refuses.
//         Q2 -- Reset at EVERY turn boundary, not just Korg's own. So during opponent's turn
//               Korg gets a fresh 2-play budget for reactive Spells (Rabid Wasperine Counter-
//               attack, Jingjack, Spirit Spells, Fate's Whimsy plays, etc.).
//         Q3 -- Reactive Spells Korg plays during opponent's turn DO count against the current
//               turn's budget (which is fresh per Q2).
//
//   "Zet: Whenever one of your Creatures attacks, once per attack, one of your other Creatures may
//   join in the attack. The defending Creature's player chooses one of your attacking Creatures to
//   lose energy in the attack." BUILT 2026-08-13 (Bucket C closure, deferred-list re-audit + owner
//   Q&A + judge ruling) via a NEW `canJointAttackViaZet` hook on registry.ts + a new
//   `AttackDeclaration.coAttackerViaZet` field in combat.ts, deliberately separate from Pack Hunt's
//   `canPackHunt`/`coAttackerInstanceId` pair so the two mechanisms COEXIST (see Q1/Q2 rulings
//   below). The joint-attack primitive it stacks onto was already in place (task #48, 2026-07-18,
//   Korrit/Giant Korrit's Pack Hunt); the defender-routed choice primitive was already in place
//   too (`pendingTargetChoice.answeringPlayerId`, PvP Step 3.5 sweep 2026-08-02, Rolling Baldar /
//   Sarazen Guard). This closure adds the specifically-Zet-shaped preview
//   (`previewZetCounterVictimChoice`) that assembles the eligible-attackers pool from the
//   declaration's already-picked joint-attack Creatures, and the damage-time counter router in
//   `declareAttack` that reads the answer back from `preCombatTargetChoices` keyed by this Magi's
//   own instance id.
//
// Owner Q&A rulings + judge ruling this build encodes (2026-08-13):
//   Q1 (Pack Hunt Korrit + Zet interaction) + judge ruling (Amanax / Technomagus screenshot):
//     "A Korrit can pack hunt along with Zet for three creatures ganging up on one, and the Korrit
//     is excluded from losing any energy in the attack." Both mechanisms COEXIST -- Korrit's Pack
//     Hunt immunity STANDS in parallel to Zet, and the Zet co-attacker is a THIRD Creature added
//     on top. `previewZetCounterVictimChoice` excludes the Pack Hunt Korrit from the counter-victim
//     pool for exactly this reason; the pool contains the Pack Hunt co-attacker + the Zet
//     co-attacker only.
//   Q2 (canPackHunt vs. a new hook): Adding a distinct `canJointAttackViaZet` hook cleanly
//     separates the two flavors' semantics -- Pack Hunt is a per-Creature grant with primary
//     immunity hardcoded; Zet is a Magi-wide grant where the defender picks who takes counter.
//     Piggybacking on `canPackHunt` would have mashed the two immunity rules together.
//   Q3 (fallback if defender doesn't answer the choice): Defender picks; if unanswered, the auto-
//     pick is the co-attacker (Pack Hunt-like default). When Pack Hunt is also invoked, that means
//     the Pack Hunt co-attacker takes counter (matches the pre-existing Pack Hunt default); when
//     only Zet is invoked, that means the Zet co-attacker takes counter -- Zet defaults to Pack-
//     Hunt-like semantics under silence, per the printed text's spirit ("The defending Creature's
//     player CHOOSES," so a non-choice hands the natural default to the attacker's side).
//   Q4 (once-per-attack scope): Attacker-OPTIONAL per attack. Zet is invoked by setting
//     `AttackDeclaration.coAttackerViaZet`; omitting it produces a normal 1v1 attack. The
//     attacker chooses each attack whether to invoke Zet, and if so with which ally.
//   Rabid Wasperine follow-up ruling: Zet fires on counter-attacks too. Since
//     `canJointAttackViaZet` is a per-attack legality check with no once-per-turn tracking, any
//     attack the granter's controller declares -- including a Rabid-Wasperine-triggered follow-up
//     inside another attack's afterCombat -- can carry a `coAttackerViaZet`. No extra plumbing
//     needed for this; the natural composition just works.
//
// Damage / counter math (Bucket C, 2026-08-13):
//   - All attackers (primary + coAttacker + coAttackerViaZet) each deal their own snapshotted
//     energy to the defender in parallel, routed through `applyCombatCounterLoss` so
//     BURROWED/Mirror Shield/reductions/etc. all apply per attacker.
//   - Counter-victim resolution:
//       - Zet only (no Pack Hunt): defender picks between [primary, coAttackerViaZet]; fallback =
//         coAttackerViaZet. Chosen victim takes defender's snapshot counter; other is immune this
//         attack.
//       - Zet + Pack Hunt: defender picks between [coAttacker, coAttackerViaZet]; primary Korrit
//         is immune per its own rule (unless Garan/T'lok/Rayje's Sword suppression fires, matching
//         Pack Hunt's own 2026-07-19 suppression pattern). Fallback = coAttacker.
//       - Pack Hunt only (no Zet): unchanged -- primary Korrit immune, coAttacker takes counter.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Korg & Zet', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing. Korg owns both `restrictsOwnPlayOf` (Relic-block) AND
  // `restrictsOwnPlayCountAt` (2-per-turn cap, Batch B 2026-08-13). Zet owns the joint-attack
  // grant.
  effectHooks: {
    Korg: ['restrictsOwnPlayOf', 'restrictsOwnPlayCountAt'],
    Zet: ['canJointAttackViaZet'],
  },
  restrictsOwnPlayOf: (state, cardDb, playerId, self, playedDef) => playedDef.card_type === 'Relic',
  restrictsOwnPlayCountAt: () => 2,
  // Zet: Magi-wide broadcast granting the joint-attack. combat.ts's `isLegalAttack` + `declareAttack`
  // read this via `effectsFor` -- so lockdown / Rayje suppression / etc. on this Magi automatically
  // disables Zet the same way it disables every other Magi Effect, no explicit gating needed here.
  // Same "always true when this Magi's Effect is live" shape as Korrit's `canPackHunt: () => true`.
  canJointAttackViaZet: () => true,
});
