// Colossus -- "Anti-Magic": two clauses.
//   1. "Colossus may not be affected by opposing Spells, Powers or Effects that specifically discard
//      Creatures from play." -> registry.ts's canBeDiscardedFromPlay (opposing-caused discard-from-
//      play immunity), the crystalParmalag/gateToOmbor `() => false` shape.
//   2. "Your Spells, Powers, and Effects may not alter the amount of energy on Colossus, or prevent
//      Colossus from losing energy." Per errata: "Your cards can not add or remove energy to Colossus
//      or allow a Rearrange to include Colossus." -> registry.ts's locksOwnControllerEnergyChange,
//      a SELF-side lock consulted by effects.ts's addEnergy/discardEnergy/rearrangeEnergy: a
//      card-caused change by Colossus's OWN controller is skipped. Opposing energy changes and all
//      combat energy loss are unaffected (combat loss never routes through these functions).
//      NOTE: the narrower "prevent Colossus from losing energy" sub-clause (your protective shields
//      failing to save it) is not modelled -- a niche interaction with no clean choke point; the
//      observable add/remove/rearrange lock is what this hook covers.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Colossus', {
  canBeDiscardedFromPlay: () => false,
  locksOwnControllerEnergyChange: () => true,
});
