// Sorreah -- "Suppress: Effects and Powers on other Magi may not be used." A passive, always-on
// blanket suppression while Sorreah is in play as any player's active Magi. Printed text has no
// "opposing" qualifier, so this reads literally per the project's standing "read literally unless
// nonsensical" convention -- blocks every OTHER Magi in the game (both sides in constructed 1v1,
// which is one opposing Magi in practice since each player has at most one active Magi).
//
// POWERS half: registry.ts's `blocksPowerUse`. Powers have a single choke point (`usePower`); a
// per-user gate is the standard hook shape. Same shape as Sorreah, Warrior's Dream Block and
// Cactus Dryte's Deny.
//
// EFFECTS half: RESOLVED 2026-08-13 (Wave C3 of the deferred-list re-audit).
//
// Mechanism: `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive`, consulted from
// `filterOwnEffectForLockdown` -- the same single choke point Rayje's Belt's Lockdown already
// goes through. When Sorreah is any player's active Magi, every OTHER Magi's named printed
// Effects are treated as if they were Rayje-locked: fine-grained per-Effect-hook stripping if
// the target Magi declares `effectHooks`, coarse whole-card silence otherwise (identical
// fallback to how Rayje's Belt degrades). Nothing to add to Sorreah's own registry entry beyond
// the `Suppress: ['blocksPowerUse']` `effectHooks` map -- her Suppress Effect's own dual role
// (Powers via `blocksPowerUse`, Effects via the external gate) is enforced from outside her file.
//
// Sorreah's own Suppress can itself be Rayje's-Belt-locked (naming "Suppress"); when locked, the
// external gate skips her as a suppressor, same convention every other named Effect follows.
//
// Owner Q&A that shaped this closure (all 2026-08-13):
//   Q1 (what "Effects" means): anything with printed "Effect - " prefix -- an entry with a `name`
//       in the card's `effects[]` array. Traps:
//     * A Spell that grants a lingering effect (like "Stealth" Spell) is NOT suppressed. Origin
//       matters -- Spell origin != Effect origin.
//     * A Power that grants an Effect (like Grej's Toughen granting Invulnerability) IS
//       suppressed once the granted Effect starts firing as an Effect on the recipient (the
//       granted Effect is still an "Effect -"). Cross-card grant handling has a documented
//       coarseness -- see `externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive`'s header.
//     * Contrast: "Reflexes" (Effect-origin, on Lascinth) IS suppressed. "Stealth" (Spell-origin)
//       is NOT.
//   Q6 (Sorreah/Drajan joint scope): Sorreah's Effects half is a blanket per-Magi shutoff, like
//       Sandswirl's per-cast `EFFECTS_LOCKED_DOWN` -- but broadcast globally by Sorreah's presence
//       instead of one target at a time. Should follow Sandswirl's precedent, which is why we
//       reuse the same choke point (`filterOwnEffectForLockdown`) rather than inventing a new one.
//
// Shares infrastructure with Drajan's Fair -- see `drajan.ts`'s own header and
// `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive` for the shared origin-detection primitive.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Sorreah', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (C3 Q2, 2026-08-12: Taglat). Suppress is the sole printed Effect;
  // its `blocksPowerUse` hook is the Powers half. The Effects half is enforced externally by
  // `grantedEffects.ts#externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive` (no local hook to list here), and the
  // same "Suppress" name is what Rayje's Belt would name to lock BOTH halves together.
  effectHooks: {
    Suppress: ['blocksPowerUse'],
  },
  blocksPowerUse: (state, cardDb, user, powerName, self) => {
    if (user.instanceId === self.instanceId) return false;
    return cardDb.get(user.definitionKey)?.card_type === 'Magi';
  },
});
