// Aglow (Spell, Underneath, cost 2) -- "Your burrowed Creatures may attack this turn. When
// attacking this turn, your burrowed Creatures gain one energy before energy is removed."
// Underneath Spell pass, Category B (2026-07-25).
//
// Both clauses are continuous rules that must apply to Creatures burrowed AFTER this Spell
// resolves too, and Aglow is a one-shot Spell already in the discard pile by then -- so neither
// can hang off an in-play card the way Digging Goggles/Ghost Bwisp's grantsCanAttackWhileBurrowedTo
// broadcast does. Same "PlayerState field, checked generically in combat.ts" shape as Scarletsong's
// Trill/Creeping Chill; see types/state.ts's aglowUntilTurn for what reads it and where. Bound to
// the turn it was cast on ("this turn"), so state.turnNumber, compared with ===.
//
// This file therefore only arms the flag -- the two clauses themselves live at their respective
// choke points in combat.ts (isLegalAttack's burrowed gate, and the pre-ctx.locked energy block).

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Aglow', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.controllingPlayer.aglowUntilTurn = ctx.state.turnNumber;
  },
});
