// Ashio (Core Magi) -- "Weave Twist: All cards that specifically reference Core instead reference
// their own region. If a card is of multiple regions, you choose which of those regions to
// reference."
//
// Built 2026-07-24 (deferred-doc staleness audit follow-up). No LOCAL hooks -- Ashio's own effect
// never fires from Ashio's own file. Instead, `targeting.ts`'s
// `ashioAdjustedRegion(state, cardDb, region, referencingRegions)` is the shared choke point: every
// OTHER card whose own printed text names 'Core' as a literal region routes that literal through
// it, passing its OWN `regions` array. See that function's own doc comment for the full mechanism,
// the "referencing card is itself Core = no-op" reasoning, and the multi-region simplification.
//
// Scoped 2026-07-24 against the full card database: 22 cards reference 'Core' in their own text
// but ARE Core-region themselves (no-op, confirmed, not touched), 4 are multi-region including
// Core (Empress Gia, Ninibom, Statement of Core Values, Twilight Mowat -- simplified, see
// targeting.ts), and 30 genuinely change under Ashio -- see docs/CHANGELOG.md's Ashio entry for
// the full card list and per-card notes.
//
// This file's `registerCardEffect` (added 2026-08-13, Wave DD1 of the deferred coverage audit)
// registers no local hook body -- the `effectHooks: { 'Weave Twist': [] }` map exists solely to
// document Ashio's printed Effect name in the registry, matching the `Fair: []` stub Drajan uses
// (`drajan.ts`, 2026-08-13 Wave C3). Consequences of this being present:
//   * A Rayje's-Belt-locked name of "Weave Twist" now takes the fine-grained per-Effect-hook
//     stripping path in `grantedEffects.ts#filterOwnEffectForLockdown` (strips nothing local
//     since Ashio has no local Weave Twist hook) instead of the coarse whole-card silence
//     fallback -- same reasoning as Drajan's Fair stub. Since Ashio has no OTHER local hooks
//     the two paths are functionally equivalent for this card today, but the map is future-
//     proofed against Ashio ever gaining a second named Effect or unnamed printed text.
//   * Since the real Weave Twist mechanism lives outside this file's registered hooks (in
//     `ashioAdjustedRegion`), a Rayje-lock of "Weave Twist" does NOT actually stop Ashio's
//     region reversion from firing -- that's the documented external-suppression coarseness
//     inherited from every card whose effect lives outside its own `effectHooks` (see
//     `externalOwnEffectSuppressionActive`'s "Documented limitation" note). Owner-scope
//     question if it ever matters in practice.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Ashio', {
  effectHooks: {
    'Weave Twist': [],
  },
});
