// Tranquility (Spell, Arderial, cost 2) -- "Until the beginning of your next turn, all Spells,
// Powers, and Effects that would discard energy may not be played. Draw one additional card during
// your Draw Step this turn." Wave DD1 of the deferred coverage audit, 2026-08-13. Previously
// deferred in `docs/deferred-card-mechanics.md` on the grounds that "would require classifying
// EVERY Power/Spell/Effect in the database by whether its own text 'discards energy'." This
// closure builds the enabling infrastructure and defers the metadata-tagging sweep separately.
//
// CLAUSE 1 -- "Spells, Powers, and Effects that would discard energy may not be played" -- is
// modeled the same way Riptide's clause 2 handles "cards that cause opponents to discard cards
// from their hand": a declarative-static `causesEnergyDiscard?: boolean` flag on
// `CardEffectDefinition` (see registry.ts), checked at two gates: `play.ts#isLegalToPlay` for
// Spells and `power.ts#isLegalPowerUse` for Powers. Both gates scan BOTH players' fields (unlike
// Riptide, which is self-scoped per its owner ruling); Tranquility's printed text has no "you"
// qualifier on "may not be played," so it applies to any player's play regardless of which side
// cast the Spell.
//
// CLAUSE 1 SIMPLIFICATIONS (documented, not silently dropped):
//   * "Effects" (the third listed category) is NOT enforced at hook-broadcast time. Passively-
//     triggered Effects that "would discard energy" (e.g. a hypothetical damage-on-attack Effect)
//     will still fire while Tranquility is active. Gating them would require either static-
//     tagging every discard-energy Effect (same metadata-sweep concern as the "which cards
//     discard energy" question below) OR dispatching each broadcast hook through a probe layer
//     -- both non-trivial for a one-turn Spell of moderate playtest impact. Owner-review Q.
//   * "may not be PLAYED" is read as "may not be played OR used" (Powers are used, not played,
//     but the printed intent clearly includes Powers per the "Spells, Powers, and Effects"
//     preamble). Matches Riptide's own precedent of reading "may not be played or used" across
//     the Spell/Power boundary.
//
// PENDING METADATA SWEEP (owner-review Q): NO cards are tagged with `causesEnergyDiscard` at
// this landing. The tag exists and both gates work correctly, but until candidates are audited
// and tagged by an owner-approved sweep, Tranquility's ban gate is a valid no-op. Candidate
// families for the sweep include:
//   * Direct-damage Spells (Cald: Lava Blast, Sunburn, Wildfire, Thermal Blast, Firestorm, ...).
//   * Discard-Creature-type Spells and Powers (Kier's Peel-Off, Kolte's Kick, most attack-and-
//     discard Powers on Cald Creatures).
//   * Board-wide sweep Spells (Cataclysm, Cave-In, Firestorm Orish, ...).
//   * Powers whose primary text is "discard N energy from ..." (Baldar Amulet, Blast Gloves,
//     etc.).
// Not urgent -- tag when the owner has time to review the full inventory. See registry.ts's
// `causesEnergyDiscard` doc comment for the full convention and this file's Bucket C-style
// owner-review Q in the Wave DD1 report.
//
// CLAUSE 2 -- "Draw one additional card during your Draw Step this turn" -- stamps
// `PlayerState.tranquilityExtraDrawUntilTurn = state.turnNumber` at resolution. Read directly in
// `turn.ts#runDrawPhase` alongside `aubrasWisdomExtraDrawUntilTurn` (same "player-level expiry
// rather than a duration tag on a specific CardInstance" reasoning, since a one-shot Spell has
// no in-play card to hang the hook on).
//
// TIMING NOTE (clause 2, "this turn"): the six-phase turn order is energize → prs1 → attack →
// playNewCreatures → prs2 → draw. Spells default to prs1/prs2 phases, both of which fire BEFORE
// the Draw phase, so a Tranquility play always lands with the Draw Step still ahead this turn.
// A Tranquility cast reactively during the Attack step or later (via some future reactive
// window) would still see its +1 land on the same-turn Draw Step. If a future card lets a Spell
// be cast during or after the Draw Step, this +1 will silently do nothing (already past); safe
// no-op, not a bug.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Tranquility', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.controllingPlayer.tranquilityBanExpiresAfterTurnNumber = beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
    ctx.controllingPlayer.tranquilityExtraDrawUntilTurn = ctx.state.turnNumber;
  },
});
