// Deadfall (Spell, cost 3) -- "Until the beginning of your next turn, the next two Creatures
// played lose half of their starting energy, rounded up. Naroom Shadow Magi may play Deadfall."
// Naroom Spell pass, Category D (2026-07-23). No target/choice of its own -- the affected
// Creatures don't exist yet when Deadfall resolves, and the printed text has no "you play"
// qualifier (applies to the next two Creatures played by EITHER player), so this can't live on a
// specific card instance the way costSurchargeNextOwnTurn (Vertigo) does. Built as a genuinely new
// GameState-level "next N plays" counter (state.deadfallPendingCharges) -- see its own doc comment
// in types/state.ts for the full remaining-count + turn-number-expiry shape, and play.ts's
// isLegalToPlay/playCard for where it's read and consumed. "Naroom Shadow Magi may play" needs no
// extra code here -- shadow_play is a plain data field the engine's region-legality check already
// honors generically.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Deadfall', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.state.deadfallPendingCharges = { remaining: 2, expiresAfterTurnNumber: beginningOfNextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state) };
  },
});
