// Combat resolution algorithm (rules-reference.md §8).
//
// Steps 1-3 and 6-8 (declare, legality, snapshot, lock-in, simultaneous damage, zero-energy
// defeat check) are fully implemented here and correct on their own for any card with no "on
// attack" or "after combat" ability text -- which is most Creatures. Steps 4-5 and 9 ("on
// attack" / "after combat" triggered effects) fire via the card-effect registry (see
// cardEffects/registry.ts's onAttack/afterCombat) for every in-play card on both sides, not just
// the attacker/defender -- some real cards react to attacks they're not directly part of (e.g.
// Ember Hyren's "Heat Feed": "whenever one of your OTHER Creatures attacks..."). The explicit
// `hooks` parameter still exists too, mainly for tests that want to bypass the registry.

