// Tony, Returned -- "Rediscover (1): Play a Relic from any discard pile, paying all costs and
// ignoring regional restrictions." Unlike most of this batch, costs ARE still paid (just region
// is ignored) -- same cost-paying shape as Warrior's Boots, minus the region check.
//
// **RESOLVED 2026-08-13 (deferred-list re-audit, Wave C1)** via a new `whoseDiscardPile: 'any'`
// mode on `discardPileSearch` (registry.ts). Mirrors the shipped `'opposing'` mode Tomes of the
// Great Library used, widened to include the ACTING player's pile as well -- a strict union of
// both discard piles, no target pick. Owner rulings applied:
//
//   Q1 (picker layout): SPLIT into two labeled groups ("your discard pile" / "opponent's
//        discard pile") in the UI, NOT interleaved -- the side a Relic is coming from is
//        load-bearing info (an opposing-pile Relic they normally couldn't play vs. an own-pile
//        one they want back). The engine-side pool remains a flat union for driver/legality
//        purposes; the SPLIT is a UI presentation concern via Play.tsx's
//        `discardPileSearchPoolByOwner` helper. See DiscardPileSearchShape's doc comment.
//   Q2 (ownership at resolution): the played Relic enters play under TONY'S CONTROLLER, not the
//        pile owner's -- Tomes' precedent (Research plays a Spell fetched from EITHER pile under
//        the caster's control) applies verbatim. `playFromZone`'s second argument is
//        `ctx.controllingPlayer` regardless of `sourceOwner`.
//   Q3 (regional restrictions on an opposing-pile Relic): Rediscover's own "ignoring regional
//        restrictions" clause covers this identically to the own-pile case. No new plumbing.
//
// Build recipe (all four steps live below and in registry.ts/queries.ts):
//   1. `registry.ts` DiscardPileSearchShape -- `whoseDiscardPile` union widened to include `'any'`,
//      doc-commented with the split-UI ruling and the two-pile lookup requirement.
//   2. `engine/src/queries.ts#discardPileSearchPool` -- `'any'` case unions every player's
//      discard pile under the shared `withRegionSwap` wrapper, same insertion-order flattening
//      Tomes' `'opposing'` case uses.
//   3. `app/src/renderer/src/screens/Play.tsx#discardPileSearchPool` -- unions both piles for the
//      combined pool; a new `discardPileSearchPoolByOwner` helper feeds the split-labeled render
//      block, which shows two sub-sections ("your discard pile" / "opponent's discard pile") with
//      a shared checkbox budget.
//   4. Tony's `resolvePower` below -- looks the chosen id up in BOTH discard piles (mirroring
//      Tomes' own "chosen id might belong to either player's pile" split), pays Tony's Magi, and
//      hands off to `playFromZone` with the correct `sourceOwner` for the pile it came from;
//      `controllingPlayer` remains Tony's controller per Q2.
//
// "Animite Affinity: Tony may play Creatures as though he were a Magi of any region." BUILT
// 2026-07-28 (ability-count sweep). This file previously called it "the separate, already-tracked
// passive-effect gap" -- a STALE deferral: registry.ts's `regionOverride` has done exactly this
// since task #29-2e, and returning true forces the play to Free with no penalty, restrictions
// included. Re-verified rather than trusted (owner: "I am not trusting any deferral from pre-Spell
// pass at this point").
//
// **Creatures only, and that narrowness is the whole point** (owner, 2026-07-28). This is NOT a
// Jalex-style blanket grant -- Jalex covers Creatures AND Spells, and a true region override would
// also open up Relics. Tony is more precisely read as "ignores all regional penalties and
// restrictions when playing CREATURES, including ones that say Region Only." Nearest sibling is
// Yerthe's Hyren Affinity. Concretely: Statement of Core Values is a Bograth/Core-only RELIC, and
// Animite Affinity must not unlock it -- there is a test for exactly that.
//
// Tony is a Universal Magi, so two of the three behaviours are live today:
//   - off-region Creature (no shared region): normally a +1 regional penalty -> now Free.
//   - Core Creature: normally flatly ILLEGAL for a non-Core Magi -> now legal.
//   - "Only Bograth/Core Magi can play" Creatures (Gwaeg, Rous, Zungg, Tar Hyren, Twilight Mowat):
//     currently unenforced engine-wide -- `region_restrictive` is set on 12 Spells and no Creature
//     or Relic at all (see docs/plans/ability-count-sweep-2026-07-27.md). When that data gap is
//     closed this hook already covers them; nothing here needs to change.
//
// "If Tony Jones is among your defeated Magi, when you reveal Tony, Returned, add three energy to
// Tony, Returned" -- built 2026-07-12. Same reveal-time-conditional-on-defeatedMagi-history shape
// as Zet's Good Riddance/theRealQwade.ts, just scoped to the CONTROLLER's own defeatedMagi only
// (not "any player's," unlike Zet's Korg check).

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { playFromZone, addEnergy } from '../effects.js';
import { magiCountsAs } from './magiIdentity.js';

registerCardEffect('Tony, Returned', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (fixes 2026-08-12 live playtest: Rayje's Belt naming "Animite
  // Affinity" as its Lockdown pick silenced Tony's UNRELATED reveal-time +3 energy clause too,
  // via effectsWithSourceFor's whole-card fallback. That fallback fires when a card has any
  // locked printed Effect but no `effectHooks` map narrowing which hooks belong to which named
  // Effect -- Shadow Empress, Rock Yajo etc. already declare one for the same reason).
  //
  // Only Animite Affinity is a NAMED Effect on this card (see def.effects). The reveal bonus,
  // "Tony may be in a stack with Tony Jones" pairing, and Rediscover are all top-level printed
  // text OR a Power, none of which the printed-name lockdown should touch -- so they aren't
  // listed here, and `effectsWithSourceFor` keeps them live when only 'Animite Affinity' is
  // locked. Powers are already exempt at power.ts (blocksPowerUse gates them separately), but
  // listing here would be a no-op regardless -- effectHooks only narrows what a lockdown or
  // Taglat grant carries, it doesn't ADD hooks.
  effectHooks: {
    'Animite Affinity': ['regionOverride'],
  },
  discardPileSearch: {
    count: 1,
    // 'any' -- union of BOTH players' discard piles into one pool (2026-08-13). The UI splits
    // this into two labeled groups per owner ruling Q1; the engine keeps a flat pool for
    // driver/legality purposes. See registry.ts's DiscardPileSearchShape doc comment.
    whoseDiscardPile: 'any',
    filter: (state, cardDb, playerId, card) => cardDb.get(card.definitionKey)?.card_type === 'Relic',
  },
  resolvePower: (ctx) => {
    if (ctx.powerName !== 'Rediscover') return;
    const ids = ctx.chosenDiscardPileIds ?? [];
    if (ids.length !== 1) return;
    const [id] = ids;
    // "any discard pile" -- the chosen id might belong to EITHER player's pile. Mirror Tomes'
    // two-pile lookup (see tomesOfTheGreatLibrary.ts's resolvePower). `sourceOwner` is whichever
    // pile the Relic actually came from; the played Relic still enters play under Tony's
    // controller (owner ruling Q2, 2026-08-13, and Tomes' own precedent for a Spell fetched from
    // an opposing pile).
    let sourceOwner: typeof ctx.controllingPlayer | undefined;
    let card;
    for (const holder of ctx.state.players.values()) {
      const found = holder.discardPile.find((c) => c.instanceId === id);
      if (found) {
        sourceOwner = holder;
        card = found;
        break;
      }
    }
    if (!sourceOwner || !card) return;
    const def = ctx.cardDb.get(card.definitionKey);
    const magi = ctx.controllingPlayer.activeMagi;
    if (!def || def.card_type !== 'Relic' || !magi || typeof def.cost !== 'number') return;
    if ((magi.currentEnergy ?? 0) < def.cost) return;

    magi.currentEnergy = (magi.currentEnergy ?? 0) - def.cost;
    playFromZone(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, { owner: sourceOwner, zone: 'discardPile', instanceId: id! }, ctx.controllingPlayer, null, ctx.rng);
  },
  // Animite Affinity. Creature-only by design -- see the header. `contributor === magi` because
  // this is Tony's own passive about his own plays, not something he grants to other cards.
  regionOverride: (state, cardDb, playedDef, magi, contributor) => {
    if (contributor.instanceId !== magi.instanceId) return false;
    return playedDef.card_type === 'Creature';
  },
  onMagiRevealed: (state, cardDb, revealedMagi, self) => {
    if (revealedMagi.instanceId !== self.instanceId) return;
    const player = state.players.get(self.controllerId);
    if (!player) return;
    if (player.defeatedMagi.some((m) => magiCountsAs(cardDb, m, 'Tony Jones'))) {
      addEnergy(state, cardDb, self, 3, 'effect');
    }
  },
});
