// Lightning Sand (Spell, Bograth/d'Resh) -- "Until the beginning of your next turn, the first
// time one of your cards is chosen for an opposing Power or attack, the opposing Power does
// nothing, or your defending Creature loses no energy in the attack."
//
// No target, no choice -- resolveSpell just arms a new player-level shared charge
// (`PlayerState.lightningSandChargeUntilTurn`, types/state.ts) consumed by whichever of two
// choke points fires first: `power.ts#usePower` (an opposing Power targeting one of your cards --
// the whole Power does nothing, cost still paid) or `combat.ts#applyCombatCounterLoss` (your
// defending Creature loses no energy in that one attack). See the field's own doc comment for the
// full design -- closest existing precedent is `tryConsumeFirstOpposingLossShield` (Baby Furok)
// for the "shared charge spent by whichever of N choke points fires first" shape, but that one
// resets every turn; this persists across turns until spent or its own expiry passes.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { nextOwnTurnNumber } from '../durationTags.js';

registerCardEffect('Lightning Sand', {
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    ctx.controllingPlayer.lightningSandChargeUntilTurn = nextOwnTurnNumber(ctx.state);
  },
});
