// Wind Hyren -- "Invigorate: Increase your Arderial or d'Resh Magi's Energize by two. A Magi
// can only be affected by one Invigorate at a time." The +2 grant (to your own Magi, only if
// it's Arderial or d'Resh) is implemented below.
//
// BUILT 2026-08-13 (Bucket D closure, Batch A): the stacking-cap ("A Magi can only be affected
// by one Invigorate at a time") is now enforced by `turn.ts#effectiveEnergizeRate`. Owner
// ruling (2026-08-13, this batch): "applying whatever energize increase is the highest of the
// 'invigorate' effects and silencing the rest." Read as a global game rule active whenever any
// live Wind Hyren is in play, not just Wind-Hyren-scoped.
//
// Mechanism: `energizeRateModifier` contributions whose SOURCE effect declares
// `effectHooks: { Invigorate: [...] }` are bucketed separately during the summing loop; when
// any live Wind Hyren is in play (checked via `effectsFor` so Rayje-lockdown of Invigorate
// silences the cap along with the +2 grant), `Math.max` of the bucket is added instead of the
// sum. All 5 continuous-Invigorate cards in the corpus now declare the `effectHooks` annotation:
// Wind Hyren (this file), Thast, Water of Life, Rayje's Construct, Ruid. Tree Hinko's
// Invigorate is a one-shot Power (uses `applyEnergizeModifier`, not the continuous broadcast)
// and is deliberately excluded from the cap -- the printed cap text is about continuous
// "affected by" state, not about individual +N events.
//
// Global scope note: the cap applies to ALL Magis while Wind Hyren is out, not just Arderial
// or d'Resh Magis. Wind Hyren's own +2 grant is region-gated (only fires for Arderial/d'Resh
// Magis), but the cap ITSELF -- "A Magi can only be affected by one Invigorate at a time" --
// is a general rule that fires for any Magi with 2+ live Invigorate contributions once Wind
// Hyren is in play. Example: p2 has a Bograth Magi + Ruid + Water of Life; Wind Hyren on p1
// makes p2's Magi's Invigorate contributions collapse to +1 (the higher of the two) instead
// of +2.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Wind Hyren', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (2026-08-13 Batch A). Invigorate owns the energizeRateModifier
  // hook -- the annotation is load-bearing here, since turn.ts#effectiveEnergizeRate reads it
  // to identify this contribution as eligible for the Wind Hyren global stacking cap.
  effectHooks: {
    Invigorate: ['energizeRateModifier'],
  },
  energizeRateModifier: (state, cardDb, energizing, self) => {
    const owner = state.players.get(self.controllerId);
    if (owner?.activeMagi?.instanceId !== energizing.instanceId) return 0;
    const magiDef = cardDb.get(energizing.definitionKey);
    if (!magiDef?.regions.includes('Arderial') && !magiDef?.regions.includes("d'Resh")) return 0;
    return 2;
  },
});
