/**
 * Engine-visible reactive offers (task #591+, 2026-07-30) -- the architecture behind bot mode and
 * future networked PvP both needing to see a card's negotiable reaction (power/spell negation,
 * Furok protection, target redirect, target protection, the pre-attack defender-substitution
 * chain) as real `GameState`, not a Play.tsx-only prompt. Full context/rationale lives in the
 * approved plan (see PROGRESS.md's 2026-07-30 entry and docs/CHANGELOG.md); this file's own header
 * tracks just the mechanical roadmap.
 *
 * Roadmap (each phase adds stages to `attemptUsePower`/`attemptPlayCard`, or a new `attemptX`
 * entry point, without touching the ones already landed):
 *   Phase 1: `attemptUsePower`'s `negation` stage, `attemptPlayCard`'s `spellNegation` stage --
 *     the proving case, one Shape-A mechanism per entry point.
 *   Phase 2: the remaining Shape-A mechanisms -- `furokProtection` on both entry points,
 *     `attachedSpellNegation` and `discardSave` on `attemptPlayCard`.
 *   Phase 3: `attemptDeclareAttack` -- the Shape-D pre-attack chain (hide / discard-and-play /
 *     redirect / co-defense), a THIRD `attemptKind` alongside `usePower`/`playCard`.
 *   Phase 4: Shape-B two-step target redirect (Refract) -- `targetRedirectOffer` (pick a
 *     redirecting card, or decline) followed by `targetRedirectTarget` (pick that card's own
 *     replacement target) on both `attemptUsePower` and `attemptPlayCard`.
 *   Phase 5 (here): Shape-C hard-block power-target-protection (Swirling Orshaa's Morph) --
 *     `attemptUsePower`'s `targetProtection` stage, checked FIRST (ahead of even
 *     `targetRedirectOffer`). The one stage in the whole file where accepting ABORTS the attempt
 *     instead of continuing toward the real engine call, and where `pool` holds creature TYPE NAMES
 *     rather than candidate card ids.
 *   Phase 6: Play.tsx migrates onto these entry points; the ~14 now-dead prompt states go away.
 *
 * Every stage here calls an EXISTING, unmodified preview function (previewPowerNegationOffers,
 * previewFurokProtectionOffers, findAttachedSpellNegationOffers, ...) -- this file adds a pause
 * point in front of the real `usePower`/`playCard`/`declareAttack` call, it does not reimplement
 * any detector or resolver.
 *
 * Multi-stage sequencing (new as of Phase 2): a single attempt can have several stages to check in
 * order (mirroring Play.tsx's `finishUsePower`/`finishPlayCard` chained prompt checks). Rather than
 * looping inline, each `attemptX` call checks the FIRST not-yet-checked stage with a live pool,
 * pauses on it, and `resolveReactiveOffer` re-enters `attemptX` with that stage appended to
 * `checkedStages` -- so a decline (or an accept, which doesn't stop the action for these Shape-A
 * mechanisms) still lets a LATER stage in the ordered list get its own chance, exactly like
 * Play.tsx's chain of `if (offers.length > 0) { ...; return }` checks does today.
 */

