// Owinda's Gift (Spell, Orothe, cost 3) -- "If you have a Creature in play, draw four cards. Return
// any one of your Creatures in play to your hand, discarding all of that Creature's energy." Orothe
// Spell pass, Category B (2026-07-24). The "if you have a Creature in play" condition and "return
// any ONE of your Creatures" target describe the same pool -- spellTargets' own pool (own Creatures
// in play) is empty exactly when the condition fails, so an empty pool naturally fizzles the whole
// Spell (no draw either), matching this project's established "if you control X" whiff pattern.
// returnToHand (effects.ts) already discards the returned Creature's energy as part of leaving play.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';
import { creaturesControlledBy } from '../targeting.js';
import { drawCards, returnToHand } from '../effects.js';

registerCardEffect("Owinda's Gift", {
  spellTargets: (state, cardDb, playerId) => creaturesControlledBy(state, cardDb, playerId),
  resolveSpell: (ctx) => {
    if (!ctx.chosenTargetId) return;
    const target = creaturesControlledBy(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, ctx.controllingPlayer.playerId).find(
      (c) => c.instanceId === ctx.chosenTargetId
    );
    if (!target) return;
    drawCards(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, ctx.controllingPlayer, 4);
    returnToHand(ctx.state, ctx.cardDb, ctx.controllingPlayer, target.instanceId);
  },
});
