// Tony At A Con (Magi, PR/Promo, Universal) -- "Caffeine!: Take an additional turn after this one.
// All Magi in your Magi stack gain 'Effect -- Sleep Dep: At the end of your turn, if you just took
// two turns in a row, defeat your Magi. Sleep Dep cannot be prevented or canceled.'"
//
// Category D SIXTH item, 2026-08-12. Owner rulings (2026-08-12) drove the whole build:
//   Q1: Extra turn is treated as Tony's next own turn -- standard `sweepExpiredDurationTags` at
//       start of the extra turn correctly clears tags whose expiry was "until end of my (normal)
//       turn." A documented edge remains: tags applied on Tony's normal turn with expiry
//       `nextOwnTurnNumber` (N+2) linger through both the extra turn AND the following opponent
//       turn -- one turn of over-coverage. Not fixed here; fixing it would break opponent-scoped
//       tags Tony applied on the same normal turn (they'd get swept before opponent's actual next
//       turn). See CURRENT-INVESTIGATION.md and this file's "Duration-tag edge" section below.
//   Q2: Grant Sleep Dep to `activeMagi` + every Magi still in `magiQueue` at Caffeine!'s
//       resolution. "All Magi in your Magi stack" = the untapped succession queue plus the
//       currently-active Magi. Defeated Magi are NOT granted -- they're never coming back and the
//       grant is text-scoped to future Magi that will still take turns.
//   Q3: Sleep Dep only fires at end of a turn if `justTookAdditionalTurn` was set at the START of
//       that turn (i.e., THIS turn was an extra turn). After the extra turn ends, the opponent
//       takes their normal turn, and Tony's next turn after that is NOT "two in a row," so Sleep
//       Dep does not fire again for that natural sequence.
//   Q4: Chained Caffeine! is legal. If Tony casts Caffeine! on his extra turn, he earns ANOTHER
//       extra turn -- at end of the first extra turn, Sleep Dep defeats Tony (Magi #1); the
//       succession Magi is revealed for the SECOND extra turn (still `hasSleepDep` from the
//       original grant); at end of the second extra turn, Sleep Dep defeats that Magi too. Two
//       Magi lost.
//   Q5: Direct `defeatMagi` bypasses Spirit of Rayje's pre-defeat interrupt naturally, because
//       the interrupt is only offered from `checkMagiDefeats`'s zero-energy check path -- Sleep
//       Dep calls `defeatMagi` directly (through `turn.ts#runEndOfTurnHooks`), same as Golthub/
//       Trug/The Real Qwade. Lockdown from Rayje's Belt or similar can NAME "Sleep Dep" as the
//       locked-down Effect, but Sleep Dep is implemented as a direct engine check (a boolean
//       `hasSleepDep` flag read by `runEndOfTurnHooks` before Sleep Dep triggers), NOT via the
//       `effectsFor` dispatch that `isCardEffectLockedDown` gates -- so the lockdown never
//       actually reaches Sleep Dep's firing site.
//   Q6: The extra turn is a brand-new, out-of-sequence turn. It energizes normally --
//       `skipEnergizeForFirstTurn` is a turn-1-specific flag never set again after game start, so
//       the extra turn goes through the normal `runEnergizePhase` path like any other turn.
//
// FIELDS ADDED for this build:
//   `PlayerState.pendingExtraTurns: number` -- incremented per Caffeine! cast, decremented and
//     consumed by `turn.ts#completeTurnHandoff` (which skips rotation while > 0).
//   `PlayerState.justTookAdditionalTurn: boolean` -- set at the start of an extra turn (in
//     `completeTurnHandoff`'s extra-turn branch), read by `runEndOfTurnHooks` for the Sleep Dep
//     trigger, cleared at the end of that same turn.
//   `CardInstance.hasSleepDep: boolean` -- stamped on every Magi in Tony's stack at Caffeine!'s
//     resolution, permanent (no expiry); read by `runEndOfTurnHooks` alongside
//     `justTookAdditionalTurn` as the direct Sleep Dep gate.
//
// PLACEMENT: Sleep Dep's actual firing site is in `turn.ts#runEndOfTurnHooks` (right after the
// end-of-turn sweeps, before `turnHandoffPending` is set). That's a DELIBERATE choice, not
// laziness -- see the "Q5 bypass" reasoning above. Anything routed through `effectsFor` or
// `checkMagiDefeats` would silently pick up preventions this ruling forbids.
//
// TONY JONES (Tony At A Con's base printing) has its own separate registry entry in `tonyJones.ts`;
// TONY, RETURNED (the post-defeat printing) has its own in `tonyReturned.ts`. The three share
// only an `alternate` link in the DB, not text -- see `leagueElder.ts`'s doc comment for why
// that link is deliberately not general effect inheritance.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Tony At A Con', {
  resolvePower: (ctx) => {
    if (ctx.powerName !== 'Caffeine!') return;
    const player = ctx.controllingPlayer;
    player.pendingExtraTurns += 1;
    // Stamp Sleep Dep on every Magi still available in the stack (Q2). The active Magi (Tony
    // himself) always gets the flag; every queued Magi does too, so post-defeat replacements
    // still carry it -- required for the chained-Caffeine! case (Q4) where the follow-up extra
    // turn's replacement Magi must ALSO trigger Sleep Dep. Idempotent: re-granting from a second
    // Caffeine! cast just sets the same `true` again.
    if (player.activeMagi) player.activeMagi.hasSleepDep = true;
    for (const queued of player.magiQueue) queued.hasSleepDep = true;
  },
});
