// Baby Furok -- "Cuddly-Wuddly: The first opposing Spell, Power, Effect, or attack that removes
// energy from Baby Furok during each opposing Player's turn removes no energy from it." Built task
// #45, 2026-07-18, the Naroom region pass.
//
// TURN-GATED, not merely source-based (corrected 2026-07-26 after a live playtest: Baby Furok
// attacked into Yaromant on its OWN turn and took no counter-damage). The shield only exists during
// an OPPOSING player's turn, exactly as printed -- so counter-damage taken while Baby Furok is the
// attacker on its own turn is NOT absorbed.
//
// The original build was source-based and treated the printed wording as flavour. That came out of
// a conversation covering Baby Furok and Zannah together -- the first two cards of this protection
// family -- and the two cards' wordings got conflated. They are in fact BOTH opposing-turn-only:
//   * Baby Furok: "during each opposing Player's turn".
//   * Zannah's Charm: "On each opposing turn ...". Note that is Zannah's ERRATA'D text; the
//     pre-errata printing said "Each turn", and the 2i Design Team erratum is explicitly
//     "Only on opposing turns does Charm trigger" -- so the every-turn reading is the OLD card.
//     Zannah (zannah.ts) already gates correctly on activePlayerId; only Baby Furok was wrong.
//
// `state.activePlayerId !== self.controllerId` is the whole of the gate: on its controller's own
// turn the hook simply declines, and the shared per-turn charge in registry.ts's
// absorbsFirstOpposingLossPerTurn is never consumed. Both energy-loss code paths (effects.ts's
// discardEnergy for Spell/Power/Effect, combat.ts's step-7 for attacks and counter-damage) run
// through that one charge -- see the hook's own doc comment.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

registerCardEffect('Baby Furok', {
  absorbsFirstOpposingLossPerTurn: (state, _cardDb, self) => state.activePlayerId !== self.controllerId,
});
