// All-High King Korg -- Effects:
//   Super Clever: "Korg cannot play Relics" -- built this pass (task #30, 2026-07-15) via
//   registry.ts's new restrictsOwnPlayOf, with a named exception carved out for his own two
//   signature Relics (Korg's Sceptre's "No Moving Parts," Korg's Poetry's "One-Syllable Words":
//   "Korg can play [this]"). Korg & Zet's similar-but-not-identical "may not play Relics" (bundled
//   with an unrelated 2-cards-per-turn cap) is a DIFFERENT card/file, not covered here.
//   Super Brave: "Whenever Korg has no energy, he is defeated, even if he has Creatures in play."
// Text: "Korg can only play Core, Bograth, and Universal cards." Needs NO code -- Korg's own
// `regions` field is already ['Core', 'Bograth'], and regions.ts's `checkRegionLegality` (task
// #35, 2026-07-16 fix) now grants a Core-inclusive Magi free access to cards matching ANY of
// their own listed regions, not just Core, so "only Core/Bograth/Universal" is already exactly
// what the generic engine produces -- no Relic, no off-region Creature/Spell (all of which would
// need Universal or a shadow_play grant to reach him) can slip through.
//
// Also grants regionOverride for those same two signature Relics -- kept even after the
// regions.ts fix above, since Korg's Sceptre/Poetry (Bograth-only Relics) still need a full
// override to ignore the region *penalty* Bograth cards would otherwise pay if this weren't
// present... actually the regions.ts fix already makes them tier-2 (free, no penalty) automatically,
// same as any other Bograth card under Korg now, but this regionOverride is left in place as a
// harmless no-op rather than risk pulling threads on Korg's own Relic-restriction interaction
// (Super Clever's RELIC_EXCEPTIONS carve-out reads this file's OWN restrictsOwnPlayOf, not
// region legality, so the two mechanisms are independent regardless). Deliberately placed HERE,
// on the Magi's own file, not on the two Relics' own files -- play.ts's regionOverride broadcast
// only scans the active Magi + already-in-play cards, never the player's hand, so a Relic
// granting itself the override while it's still the card being played would never fire.
//
// Super Brave drops the normal "0 energy AND 0 Creatures" Magi-defeat check's Creature-count
// requirement entirely -- registry.ts's `customDefeatCondition` hook (2026-07-12), checked by
// energy.ts's checkMagiDefeats INSTEAD OF the normal condition.

import { registerCardEffect } from './registry.js';

const RELIC_EXCEPTIONS = new Set(["Korg's Sceptre", "Korg's Poetry"]);

registerCardEffect('All-High King Korg', {
  // Per-Effect hook narrowing (E1, 2026-08-12). Super Clever owns the Relic-play block plus the
  // regionOverride carve-out for Korg's own two signature Relics (a coupled pair: the override
  // exists to keep the exception-list Relics playable). Super Brave owns the 0-energy defeat.
  effectHooks: {
    'Super Clever': ['restrictsOwnPlayOf', 'regionOverride'],
    'Super Brave': ['customDefeatCondition'],
  },
  customDefeatCondition: (state, cardDb, magi) => (magi.currentEnergy ?? 0) <= 0,
  restrictsOwnPlayOf: (state, cardDb, playerId, self, playedDef) =>
    playedDef.card_type === 'Relic' && !RELIC_EXCEPTIONS.has(playedDef.name),
  regionOverride: (state, cardDb, playedDef) => RELIC_EXCEPTIONS.has(playedDef.name),
});
